mathedu,mathedu:538a10c647626eec,,Measurement error,Mixes rupees and paise without converting units,ok,4.2+40 x=6.3+15 x+40,ok,"the price of commodity x increases by 40 paise every year , while the price of commodity y increases by 15 paise every year . if in 2001 , the price of commodity x was rs . 4.20 and that of y was rs . 6.30 , in which year commodity x will cost 40 paise more than the commodity y ?",Assume after $x$ years $$ \begin{aligned} & 4.2+40 x=6.3+15 x+40 \\ & 25 x=42.1 \\ & x=1.684 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#13
mathedu,mathedu:1d448b6f82a462c0,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats the area of a circular ring as circumference times its width,ok,\frac{2 \times r \times 3.14 \times 4}{r^2 \times 3.14}=\frac{11}{25},ok,"a circular swimming pool is surrounded by a concrete wall 4 ft wide . if the area of the concrete wall surrounding the pool is 11 / 25 that of the pool , then the radius of the pool is ?",radius of the pool $=r$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{2 \times r \times 3.14 \times 4}{r^2 \times 3.14}=\frac{11}{25} \\ & 11 r=25 \times 8=200 \\ & r=\frac{200}{11} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#14
