mathedu,mathedu:685d6c03ee6b79bc,,Algebraic error,Makes an arithmetic error when dividing a quantity by a denominator,ok,\frac{x}{3}=22-\frac{1}{7} x+8,ok,"the sum of two numbers is 184 . if one - third of the one exceeds one - seventh of the other by 8 , find the smaller number .","assume one number $X$, the other $(184-x)$ $$ \begin{aligned} & x \times \frac{1}{3}=\frac{1}{7}(184-x)+8 \\ & \frac{x}{3}=22-\frac{1}{7} x+8 \\ & \frac{10}{21} x=30 \\ & x=63 \end{aligned} $$ the other one: 121 $$ \text { Ans }=63 $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#33
mathedu,mathedu:786f8c7cb481e905,,Comprehension error,,label_conflict,20-4=16 \text { (pounds) },ok,a club wants to mix 20 pounds of candy worth $ 10.00 per pound with candy worth $ 5.00 per pound to reduce the cost of the mixture to $ 6.00 per pound . how many pounds of the $ 5.00 per pound candy should be used ?,"assume uses $X$ pounds 10 dollars one, then use $(20-x)$ pounds 5 dollars one $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{x \times 10+(20-x) 5}{20}=6 \\ & 10 x+100-5 x=120 \\ & 5 x=20 \\ & x=4 \\ & 20-4=16 \text { (pounds) } \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#39
