mathedu,mathedu:1f2ed676f73aae13,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Fails to divide the total passing distance by two for equal lengths,ok,\frac{10}{3.6} \times 36=100,ok,two trains of equal length are running on parallel lines in the same direction at 46 km / hr and 36 km / hr . the faster train passes the slower train in 36 seconds . the length of each train is ?,\begin{aligned} & 46 \mathrm{~km}-36 \mathrm{~km}=10 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} \\ & 10 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr}=\frac{10}{3.6} \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s} \\ & \frac{10}{3.6} \times 36=100 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#63
mathedu,mathedu:4aec24c4e25c0aff,,Careless error,Reports an answer inconsistent with the calculated value,ok,\Rightarrow & x=3 \# \end{aligned} $$ A. mary sold 6 boxes of butter cookies.,ok,"mary sold boxes of butter cookies . ann sold 5 times as much as she did . 18 boxes of cookies were sold that day , how many boxes did mary sell ?",Assume mary sold $x$ boxes of butter cookies. $$ \begin{aligned} & x+5 x=18 \\ \Rightarrow & 6 x=18 \\ \Rightarrow & x=18 \div 6 \\ \Rightarrow & x=3 \# \end{aligned} $$ A. mary sold 6 boxes of butter cookies.,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#68
mathedu,mathedu:0a2b49ba46d5348d,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Miscomputes the fraction of the total represented by the difference,ok,& \frac{x-y}{x}=\frac{2}{3},ok,"a man saves a certain portion of his income during a year and spends the remaining portion on his personal expenses . next year his income increases by 40 % but his savings increase by 100 % . if his total expenditure in 2 years is double his expenditure in 1 st year , what % age of his income in the first year did he save ?",Assume the man income $x$ and expense $y$ in the fist year $$ \begin{aligned} & 2 \times (x-y)=1.4 x-y \\ & 2 x-2 y=1.4 x-y \\ & 0.6 x=y \\ & x=\frac{5}{3} y \\ & \frac{x-y}{x}=\frac{2}{3} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#70
