mathedu,mathedu:109ad434bbbff87c,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats 1 as a prime number,ok,(1) (3) 7 (11) (13),ok,"two different primes may be said torhymearound an integer if they are the same distance from the integer on the number line . for instance , 3 and 7 rhyme around 5 . what integer r between 1 and 20 , inclusive , has the greatest number of distinct rhyming primes around it ?",(1) 2 (3) \\ (1) 3 (5) \\ (3) 5 (7) \\ (1) (3) 7 (11) (13) \\ (3) (5) 11 (17) (19) \\ (7) 13 (19) \\ Ans:7 \& 11,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#74
