mathedu,mathedu:e348c6557d7f96d0,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses selling price instead of cost price as the denominator for gain percentage,ok,\frac{y_1-x}{y_1}=10 \%,ok,"a person purchases 90 clocks and sells 40 clocks at a gain of 10 % and 50 clocks at a gain of 20 % . if he sold all of them at a uniform profit of 15 % , then he would have got rs . 40 less . the cost price of each clock is ?","let the cost of every clock $x$ dollars, $10 \%$ gain selling price = y_1,$20 \%$ gain selling price y_2,$15 \%$ gain selling price y_3 $$ \begin{array}{lll} \frac{y_1-x}{y_1}=10 \% & \frac{y_2-x}{y_2}=20 \% & \frac{y_3-x}{y_3}=15 \% \\ y_1=10 y_1-10 x & 5 y_2-5 x=y_2 & 2 y_3-20 x=3y_3 \\ 9 y_1=10 x & 4 y_2=5 x & 17 y_3=20 x \\ y_1=\frac{10}{9} x & y_2=\frac{5}{4} x & y_3=\frac{20}{17} x \end{array} $$ \begin{aligned} & \left(\frac{10}{9} x-x\right) \times 40+\left(\frac{5}{4} x-x\right) \times 50=\left(\frac{20}{17} x-x\right) \times 90+40 \\ & \frac{40}{9} x+\frac{50}{4} x=\frac{270}{17} x+40 \\ & \frac{2720+7650-9720}{612} x=40 \quad x=40 \times \frac{612}{1150}=\frac{2488}{115}(\mathrm{dollars}) \end{aligned}",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#85
mathedu,mathedu:a6409dd32625aa67,,Comprehension error,Uses one worker’s completion time instead of the combined completion time,ok,\frac{1}{\frac{11}{80}} = 7.2 \quad Ans : 8 days,ok,"it will take 16 days for mary to complete a certain task alone . she worked for 8 days before she was joined by her sister . both of them completed the remaining task in 2 and half days . if her sister had joined her when she started the task , how many days would it have taken ?",mary's speed $=\frac{1}{16}$ per day $$ \frac{1}{16} \times 8=\frac{1}{2} $$ assume sister's speed x per day $$ \begin{array}{ll} \frac{\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{1}{16}+x} =2.5  \\ \frac{1}{2}=\frac{1}{16} \times \frac{5}{2}+2.5 x  \\ 2.5 x=\frac{16}{32}-\frac{5}{32}=\frac{11}{32}  \\ x=\frac{11}{32} \times \frac{10}{25} \\  =\frac{11}{80} \\ & \frac{1}{\frac{11}{80}} = 7.2 \\ Ans : 8 days \end{array} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#88
mathedu,mathedu:cd0f8475aa7b9f20,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Stops after finding the total instead of calculating the requested difference,ok,& x=3400 \times 9 \\ & =30600(rs .),ok,"income and expenditure of a person are in the ratio 5 : 4 . if the income of the person is rs . 17000 , then find his savings ?",assume he has $y<r$. $$ \begin{aligned} & x \times \frac{5}{9}=17000 \\ & x=3400 \times 9 \\ & =30600(rs .) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#100
mathedu,mathedu:d315a549a344b5da,,Algebraic error,Calculates the square root incorrectly when solving for the scale factor,ok,x=45,ok,"sides of a rectangular park are in the ratio 3 : 2 and its area is 7350 sq m , the cost of fencing it at 50 ps per meter is ?","Assume the length is $3 x$, width is $2 x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 3 x \times 2 x=7350 \\ & 6 x^2=7350 \\ & x=45 \\ & (3 \times 45+2 \times 45) \times 2 \times 50=22500 \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#102
mathedu,mathedu:30a2a29b4cd64863,,Unfinished answer,Fails to use the solved scale factor to compute the requested amount,ok,r=30,ok,"the ratio of the amount of the oil bill for the month of february to the amount of the oil bill for the month of january was 3 : 2 . if the oil bill for february had been $ 10 more , the corresponding ratio would have been 5 : 3 . how much was the oil bill for january ?",\begin{aligned} & \text { February }=3 r \\ & \text { January }=2 r \\ & \frac{3 r+10}{2 r}=\frac{5}{3} \\ & 10 r=9 r+30 \\ & r=30 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#105
