mathedu,mathedu:312987a5daa9c845,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats a 200% increase as making one quantity twice the other,ok,(x \times 2 x) \div 3=400,ok,"the length of a rectangular floor is more than its breadth by 200 % . if rs . 400 is required to paint the floor at the rate of rs . 3 / sq m , what would be the length of the floor ?",Assume the width is $X$ $$ \begin{aligned} & (x \times 2 x) \div 3=400 \\ & 2 x^2=1200 \\ & x^2=600 \\ & x=10 \sqrt{6} \\ & 2 x=20 \sqrt{6} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#128
mathedu,mathedu:9803c216d392cb87,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Subtracts an initial time interval from a time already measured afterward,ok,\left(7-\frac{7}{5}\right) \times 35=\frac{28}{5} \times 35=196,ok,"car x began traveling at an average speed of 35 miles per hour . after 84 minutes , car y began traveling at an average speed of 42 miles per hour . when both cars had traveled the same distance , both cars stopped . how many miles did car x travel from the time car y began traveling until both cars stopped ?",\begin{aligned} & \frac{84}{60}=\frac{21}{15}=\frac{7}{5}(\mathrm{hrs}) \\ & \frac{35 \times \frac{7}{5}}{42-35}=\frac{49}{7}=7 \text { (hrs) } \\ & \left(7-\frac{7}{5}\right) \times 35=\frac{28}{5} \times 35=196 \text { (miles) } \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#134
