mathedu,mathedu:a38d5c8973999615,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats distinct outcomes as equally likely despite unequal frequencies.,ok,\frac{6}{16} =\frac{3}{8},ok,"the “ s - number ” of a number x is defined as the ones digit of 2 ^ x . antony rolls a die with 6 sides labeled with the integers from 1 to 6 , each of which has an equal probability of landing face - up . he then takes 3 ^ s , where s is the s - number of the result of his die roll , and plots 3 ^ s on a number line as the point a . finally , he repeats this entire process , this time plotting the result as the point b . what is the probability that the distance between a and b is greater than the value of b ?",\begin{aligned} & a=9 \Rightarrow\left\{\begin{array}{l} b=9 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=0 \\ b=81 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=72 \\ b=229 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=720 \\ b=6561 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=6552 \end{array}\right. \\ & a=81 \Rightarrow\left\{\begin{array}{l} b=9 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=72 \ldots (1) \\ b=81 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=0 \\ b=729 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=648 \\ b=6561 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=6480 \end{array}\right. \\ & a=729 \Rightarrow\left\{\begin{array}{l} b=9 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=720  \ldots (2)\\ b=81 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=648  \ldots (3)\\ b=729 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=0 \\ b=6561 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=5832 \end{array}\right. \\ & a=6561 \Rightarrow\left\{\begin{array}{l} b=9 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=6552 \ldots(1) \\ b=81 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=6480 \ldots(5) \\ b=729 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=5832 \ldots \text { (6) } \\ b=6561 \Rightarrow \text { distance }=0 \end{array}\right.\right. \\ & \end{aligned} \begin{aligned} \frac{6}{16} & =\frac{3}{8} \\ & =0.375 \\ & =37.5 \% \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#140
mathedu,mathedu:8e908eec0505cfb3,,Unfinished answer,Drops the squared radius when simplifying the surface-area formula,ok,e=\frac{1}{2} \times\left(4 \pi r^2\right)+3=3+4 \pi r,ok,"the surface area of a sphere is 4 π r 2 , where r is the radius of the sphere . if the area of the base of a hemisphere is 3 , what is the surface area e of that hemisphere ?",e=\frac{1}{2} \times\left(4 \pi r^2\right)+3=3+4 \pi r,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#142
mathedu,mathedu:2efd4dfac4fa4e13,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses the wrong area for corner regions created by a width increase,ok,m+64 & =m+2 x+\left(4 \times 2^2\right),ok,"a rectangular photograph is surrounded by a border that is 1 inch wide on each side . the total area of the photograph and the border is m square inches . if the border had been 3 inches wide on each side , the total area would have been ( m + 64 ) square inches . what is the perimeter of the photograph , in inches ?",assume photo's perimeter is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} m+64 & =m+2 x+\left(4 \times 2^2\right) \\ 64 & =2 x+16 \\ 2 x & =48 \\ x & =24 \text { (inches)  } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#150
mathedu,mathedu:0a6613d308729830,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses subtraction instead of the sum-of-squares identity,ok,\sqrt{267-131}=\sqrt{136},ok,sum of the squares of 3 no . ' s is 267 and the sum of their products taken two at a time is 131 . find the sum ?,\begin{aligned} & \sqrt{267-131}=\sqrt{136} \\ & 3 \times \sqrt{136}=3 \sqrt{136}=6 \sqrt{34} \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#152
mathedu,mathedu:9a0c54a67fece12a,,Algebraic error,Makes an incorrect division when isolating the variable,ok,300+x =50 \times 9,ok,a 300 m long train crosses a platform in 45 sec while it crosses a signal pole in 18 sec . what is the length of the platform ?,assume the platform's length is $x \mathrm{~m}$. $$ \begin{aligned} \frac{300}{18} & =\frac{300+x}{45} \\ 3(300+x) & =50 \times 45 \\ 300+x & =50 \times 9 \\ x & =150(\mathrm{~m}) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#153
