mathedu,mathedu:04cafd65e642dbf0,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Applies profit and loss percentages directly to reciprocal rates,ok,\frac{21-x}{21}=7 \%,ok,if a man lost 7 % by selling oranges at the rate of 21 a rupee at how many a rupee must he sell them to gain 42 % ?,"assume the cost of the orange $X$, the selling price $y$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{21-x}{21}=7 \% \\ & 21 x=14.7 \\ & x=63 \\ & \frac{y-6.3}{y}=42 \% \\ & 0.58 y=6.3 \\ & y=\frac{63}{10} \times \frac{100}{58}=\frac{315}{29} \div 10.86(rs) \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#241
