mathedu,mathedu:a0a92b46d074eead,,Arithmetical error,Calculates the product of percentage factors incorrectly,ok,120 \% \times 125 \% \times 93 \% \\ &= 195 \%,ok,"a particular store purchased a stock of turtleneck sweaters and marked up its cost by 20 % . during the new year season , it further marked up its prices by 25 % of the original retail price . in february , the store then offered a discount of 7 % . what was its profit on the items sold in february ?",\begin{aligned} & 1 \times(1+20 \%) \times(1+25 \%) \times(1-7 \%) \\ &= 120 \% \times 125 \% \times 93 \% \\ &= 195 \% \\ & \text { So the profit is } 195 \%-100 \%=95 \% \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#260
