mathedu,mathedu:ee0614e978724874,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses selling price instead of cost price as the gain-percentage denominator,ok,\frac{(0.8 x-0.36 x)}{0.8 x}=\frac{0.44 x}{0.8 x},ok,the cost price of an article is 36 % of the marked price . calculate the gain percent after allowing a discount of 20 % .,Assume the marked price is $X$ cost price : $0.36 x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & X \cdot(1-20 \%) \\ & =0.8 x \\ & \frac{(0.8 x-0.36 x)}{0.8 x}=\frac{0.44 x}{0.8 x}=\frac{44}{80}=\frac{11}{20} \\ & =55 \% \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#272
