mathedu,mathedu:92fb670f84e3a8e1,,Unfinished answer,Stops after finding a rate without computing the requested equivalent quantity,ok,x=\frac{7}{120},ok,2 men and 4 boys can complete a work in 4 days . 5 men and 6 boys can complete the same work in 3 days . the work done by 2 boys is equal to the work of how many men ?,Assume boy can finish $x$ in one day man can finish $y$ in one day $$ \begin{aligned} & 2 y+4 x=\frac{1}{4} \\ & 5 y+6 x=\frac{1}{3} \\ & 10 y+20 x=\frac{5}{4} \\ & 10 y+12 x=\frac{2}{3} \\ & 8 x=\frac{7}{15} \quad x=\frac{7}{120} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#276
mathedu,mathedu:36d7adda1a268e97,,Unfinished answer,Uses the wrong time interval when forming the total circulation,ok,circulation during 1972 - 1981,ok,the circulation for magazine p in 1971 was 4 times the average ( arithmetic mean ) yearly circulation for magazine p for the years 1972 - 1980 . what is the ratio of the circulation in 1971 to the total circulation during 1971 - 1980 for magazine p ?,$\because$ circulation in $1971=4$ time the average yearly circulation in $1972-1981$ $\therefore$ circulation in 1971 : circulation during 1972 - 1981 $$ \begin{aligned} & =4: 1 \times 9 \\ & =4: 9  \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#278
