mathedu,mathedu:affd8f89c1a66c96,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Infers individual rates from insufficient equations,ok,therefore A: B: C=2 r: 2 r: r,ok,"a and b can finish a work together in 12 days , and b and c together in 16 days . if a alone works for 5 days and then b alone continues for 7 days , then remaining work is done by c in 13 days . in how many days can c alone finish the complete work ?","12 and 16 have lcm = 4 \times 4 \times 3 = 48 \\ assume the workload in total is $48 \mathrm{r}$, and the daily workloads of $a, b, c$ are $A, B, C$ respectively. $$ \begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array} { l }  { A + B = \frac { 4 8 r } { 1 2 } } \\ { B + C = \frac { 4 8 r } { 1 6 } } \end{array} \Rightarrow \left\{\begin{array}{l} A+B=4 r \ldots(1) \\ B+C=3 r \ldots(2) \end{array}\right.\right. \\ & (1)+(2) \Rightarrow A+2 B+C=7 r \ldots (3) \\ & \because \text { (1) (2) (3) } \\ & \therefore A: B: C=2 r: 2 r: r \\ & \frac{48 r}{r}=48 \text { (days) \# } \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#307
