mathedu,mathedu:ffd047ca9544a8f6,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Calculates profit percentage using selling price instead of cost price,ok,\frac{y-604}{y}=50 \%,ok,the profit earned by selling an article for rs . 753 is equal to the loss incurred when the same article is sold for rs . 455 . what should be the sale price for making 50 % profit ?,assumes the cost $x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 753-x=x-455 \\ & 2 x=1208 \\ & x=604 \end{aligned} $$ assume the selling price $y$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{y-604}{y}=50 \% \\ & 0.5 y=604 \\ & y=1208(rs) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#373
