mathedu,mathedu:8538edda54a04c4e,,Comprehension error,Uses the wrong amount when relating combined rate to elapsed time,ok,\frac { w } { X + Y } = 3,ok,"running at their respective constant rates , machine x takes 2 days longer to produce w widgets than machine y . at these rates , if the two machines together produce 5 / 4 w widgets in 3 days , how many days would it take machine x alone to produce 1 w widgets ?","assume the daily workload of machine $x, y$ is $X$ and $Y$ respectively. $$ \begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array} { l }  { \frac { w } { X } = \frac { W } { Y } + 2 } \\ { \frac { w } { X + Y } = 3 } \end{array} \Rightarrow \left\{\begin{array} { l }  { X = Y + \frac { 2 } { w } } \\ { X + Y = \frac { 3 } { w } } \end{array} \Rightarrow \left\{\begin{array}{l} X-Y=\frac{2}{w} \ldots (1) \\ X+Y=\frac{3}{w} \ldots (2) \end{array}\right.\right.\right. \\ & \text { (1) }+ \text { (2) } \Rightarrow 2 x=\frac{5}{w} \\ & x=\frac{5}{2 w} \\ & w \times \frac{5}{2 w}=\frac{5}{2} \text { (days) \# } \\ & \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#400
mathedu,mathedu:093c59ac8e7edd48,,Algebraic error,Incorrectly scales fractional terms when clearing decimal denominators,ok,\frac{x}{9.8}+\frac{x}{6.2}=2 \; \stackrel{\times 10}{\Rightarrow} \frac{x}{98}+\frac{x}{62}=20,ok,"a man can row 8 kmph in still water . when the river is running at 1.8 kmph , it takes him 2 hour to row to a place and back . what is the total distance traveled by the man ?",the speed of going to the place $\Rightarrow 8+1.8=9.8 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr}$ the speed of back from the place $$ \Rightarrow 8-1.8=6.2 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} $$ Assume the distance to the place is $X$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{x}{9.8}+\frac{x}{6.2}=2 \\ & \stackrel{\times 10}{\Rightarrow} \frac{x}{98}+\frac{x}{62}=20 \stackrel{\times 98}{\Rightarrow} x+\frac{98 x}{62}=1960 \\ & \stackrel{x 31}{\Rightarrow} 31 x+49 x=60760 \\ & \Rightarrow 80 x=60760 \Rightarrow x=60760 \div 80=759.5 \mathrm{~km} \\ & 759.5 \times 2=1519 \mathrm{~km}  \\ & \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#410
