mathedu,mathedu:e1810a8f9022fd52,,Comprehension error,Includes the middle term when summing squares of the extremes,ok,(2 x)^2+(3 x)^2+(4 x)^2=180,ok,"3 numbers are in the ratio of 2 : 3 : 4 . if the sum of the squares of the extremes is 180 , then the middle number is :","assume the three numbers are $2 X, 3 X, 4 X$ $$ \begin{aligned} & (2 x)^2+(3 x)^2+(4 x)^2=180 \\ & 29 x^2=180 \\ & x=\sqrt{\frac{180}{29}} \end{aligned} $$ middle number $=3 x$ $$ =3 \sqrt{\frac{180}{29}} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#509
