mathedu,mathedu:c072a7278e86e1aa,,Unfinished answer,Confuses the remaining price fraction with the discount rate,ok,x=\frac{105}{175}=0.6=60 \\%,ok,a merchant marks goods up by 75 % and then offers a discount on the marked price . the profit that the merchant makes after offering the discount is 5 % . what % discount did the merchant offer ?,Assume the cost price is 100 \& the discount is $X$. $100 \times(1+75 \%)=175 \Rightarrow$ marked price $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{(175 \cdot x)-100}{100}=5 \% \\ & \Rightarrow 175 x-100=5 \\ & \Rightarrow 175 x=105 \\ & \Rightarrow x=\frac{105}{175}=0.6=60 \% \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#598
