mathedu,mathedu:f492c707d6a76de4,,Algebraic error,Makes an arithmetic error when solving a linear equation,ok,2 x=65 \quad x=37.5,ok,"in an election between two candidates a and b , the number of valid votes received by a exceeds those received by b by 15 % of the total number of votes polled . if 20 % of the votes polled were invalid and a total of 8720 votes were polled , then how many valid votes did b get ?",\begin{aligned} &\text { assume } b \text { got } x \% \text { valid votes. }\\ &\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c}  & a & b & \text { invalid } & \text { total } \\ \hline \% & (x+15) \% & x \% & 20 \% & 100 \% \end{array} \\ x+15+x=100-20 \\ 2 x=65 \\ x=37.5 \\ 8720 \times 37.5 \%=3270\end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#615
mathedu,mathedu:eee0e53707d43206,,Comprehension error,Divides one component's hours by another component's hours instead of total hours,ok,\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{7}{5} t \div\left(\frac{2}{3} \times t\right),ok,"company t produces two kinds of stereos : basic and deluxe . of the stereos produced by company t last month , 2 / 3 were basic and the rest were deluxe . if it takes 7 / 5 as many hours to produce a deluxe stereo as it does to produce a basic stereo , then the number of hours it took to produce the deluxe stereos last month was what fraction of the total number of hours it took to produce all the stereos ?",Let the company need $t$ horts to produce basic stereo $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{7}{5} t \div\left(\frac{2}{3} \times t\right) \\ = & \frac{7}{15} t \div \frac{2}{3} t \\ = & \frac{7}{10} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#616
