mathedu,mathedu:82db698b30f3d576,,Unfinished answer,Stops after finding the quantities instead of giving their ratio,ok,x=12 \Rightarrow y=18,ok,a 30 kg metal bar made of alloy of tin and silver lost 3 kg of its weight in the water . 10 kg of tin loses 1.375 kg in the water ; 5 kg of silver loses 0.375 kg . what is the ratio of tin to silver in the bar ?,assume the metal bar made of $x \mathrm{~kg}$ of tin and $y \mathrm{~kg}$ of silver. $$ \left\{\begin{array} { l }  { x + y = 3 0 } \\ { \frac { 1 . 3 7 5 x } { 1 0 } + \frac { 0 . 3 7 5 y } { 5 } = 3 } \end{array} \Rightarrow \left\{\begin{array} { l }  { x + y = 3 0 } \\ { 1 . 3 7 5 x + 0 . 7 5 y = 3 0 } \end{array} \Rightarrow \left\{\begin{array}{l} x+y=30 \ldots(1) \\ 11 x+6 y=240 \ldots(2) \end{array}\right.\right.\right. $$ substitute $(30-x)$ for $y$ in (2) $$ \begin{aligned} 11 x+6(30-x) & =240 \\ 5 x & =60 \\ x & =12 \Rightarrow y=18 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#680
