mathedu,mathedu:7af08977accd2126,,Comprehension error,Uses the multiplier as the quotient instead of multiplying it by the difference,ok,x \div 1000=2 ldots 70,ok,a no . when divided by the sum of 555 and 445 gives 2 times their difference as quotient & 70 as remainder . find the no . is ?,$$ 555+445=1000 $$ Assume the no is $x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & x \div 1000=2 \ldots 70 \\ & \Rightarrow x=2 \times 1000+70=2070 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#683
mathedu,mathedu:243a8d664b27c725,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Computes the final difference from the original quantities,ok,60-20 =40,ok,"on a certain farm the ratio of horses to cows is 6 : 1 . if the farm were to sell 15 horses and buy 15 cows , the ratio of horses to cows would then be 3 : 1 . after the transaction , how many more horses than cows would the farm own ?",\begin{aligned} &6 x-15: x+15=3: 1\\ &\begin{aligned} 3 x+45 & =6 x-15 \\ 3 x & =60 \\ x=20 & \\ 60-20 & =40 \end{aligned} \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#690
