mathedu,mathedu:81fca9b23802e366,,Unfinished answer,Does not convert the calculated work fraction into the requested monetary share,ok,\frac{x}{2} \div x=\frac{1}{2}=0.5=50 \%,ok,"a and b undertake to do a piece of work for $ 600 . a alone can do it in 6 days while b alone can do it in 8 days . with the help of c , they finish it in 3 days . find the share of a ?",assume the workload is $x$ a finish $\frac{x}{6}$ per day $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{x}{6} \times 3=\frac{x}{2} \\ & \frac{x}{2} \div x=\frac{1}{2}=0.5=50 \% \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#838
