mathedu,mathedu:4f940c1f0d861638,,Algebraic error,Miscomputes the product of speed and time by a factor of ten,ok,x =3750-160,ok,"the length of the bridge , which a train 160 meters long and travelling at 45 km / hr can cross in 30 seconds , is :",train speed: $45 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr}=45000 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{hr}=12.5 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec}$ assume bridge length is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} (160+x) \div 12.5 & =30 \\ x & =3750-160 \\ x & =3590(\mathrm{~m}) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#865
mathedu,mathedu:9bde702f35a01814,,Unfinished answer,,label_conflict,& x=225(rs),ok,"a man purchased 3 blankets @ rs . 100 each , 5 blankets @ rs . 150 each and two blankets at a certain rate which is now slipped off from his memory . but he remembers that the average price of the blankets was rs . 150 . find the unknown rate of two blankets ?",assume the unknown price is $X$ rs. $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{3 \times 100+5 \times 150+2 x}{10}=150 \\ & 1050+2 x=1500 \\ & x=225(rs) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#870
mathedu,mathedu:0bffa0949548fc9f,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Confuses the total amount lost with the final remaining amount,ok,x-0.1 x-[0.9 x-(0.9 \times 0.25) x] =5535,ok,"after 10 % of the inhabitants of a village disappeared , a panic set in during which 25 % of the remaining inhabitants left the village . at that time , the population was reduced to 5535 . what was the number of original inhabitants ?",assume the number of original inhabitants is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} x-0.1 x-[0.9 x-(0.9 \times 0.25) x] & =5535 \\ 0.9 x-0.9 x+0.225 x & =5535 \\ 0.225 x & =5535 \\ x & =24600 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#873
