mathedu,mathedu:dd6f7b446d19f569,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Calculates the commission on the markup instead of the selling price,ok,\frac{(x-19)(1-20 \%)}{19},ok,"a distributor sells a product through an online store , which take a commission of 20 % of the price set by the distributor . the distributor obtains the product from a producer at the price of $ 19 per item . what is the price that the buyer observers online if the distributor wants to maintain a 20 % profit on the cost of the item ?",assume the price on the website is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} \frac{(x-19)(1-20 \%)}{19} & =19 \times 20 \% \\ 0.8(x-19) & =19 \times 19 \times 0.2 \\ 0.8 x & =72.2+15.2=87.4 \\ x & =109.25 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#912
