mathedu,mathedu:ae0ef3b5990791aa,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses the Pythagorean theorem with an incorrect component,ok,\sqrt{\sqrt{111}^2+\sqrt{117}^2}=\sqrt{234},ok,"in the coordinate plane , one of the vertices of a square is the point ( - 6 , - 4 ) . if the diagonals of that square intersect at point ( 3 , 2 ) , what is the area of that square ?",\begin{aligned} & \sqrt{9^2+6^2}=\sqrt{117} \\ & \sqrt{\sqrt{111}^2+\sqrt{117}^2}=\sqrt{234} \\ & \sqrt{234} \cdot \sqrt{234}=234 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#946
