mathedu,mathedu:2cf01f316b58a5eb,,Unfinished answer,Fails to compute the difference between the maximum and minimum values,ok,maximum: 20-1=19 \quad \text { minimum: } 1-20=-19,ok,a ' and ' b ' are positive integers such that their lcm is 20 and their hcf is 1 . what is the difference between the maximum and minimum possible values of ' a - b ' ?,"20 's common factors: $1,2,4,5,10,20$ \begin{tabular}{c|c|c|c|c|c|c} $a$ & 1 & 2 & 4 & 5 & 10 & 20 \\ \hline$b$ & 20 & 10 & 5 & 4 & 2 & 1 \end{tabular} $a-b\left\{\begin{array}{l}\text { maximum: } 20-1=19 \\ \text { minimum: } 1-20=-19\end{array}\right.$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#968
