mathedu,mathedu:d488c199c60dd7a4,,Unfinished answer,,label_conflict,\(\frac{3}{5} x+6\right):\left(\frac{2}{5} x\right)=2: 1,ok,"in a can , there is a mixture of milk and water in the ratio 3 : 2 . if the can is filled with an additional 6 liters of milk , the can would be full and the ratio of milk and water would become 2 : 1 . find the capacity of the can ?",Assume the capacity of the can is $x$ liters. water: $\frac{2}{5} x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \left(\frac{3}{5} x+6\right):\left(\frac{2}{5} x\right)=2: 1 \\ & \Rightarrow \frac{4}{5} x=\frac{3}{5} x+6 \\ & \Rightarrow \frac{1}{5} x=6 \\ & \Rightarrow x=6 \times 5=30 \text { liters  } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#981
