mathedu,mathedu:1372185cb56ec009,,Arithmetical error,Calculates the interest rate percentage incorrectly from the annual interest.,ok,\frac{35.33}{850} = 4 \%,ok,"rs . 850 becomes rs . 956 in 3 years at a certain rate of simple interest . if the rate of interest is increased by 4 % , what amount will rs . 850 become in 3 years ?",\begin{aligned} & (956-850) \div 3 = 35.33 \\ & \frac{35.33}{850} = 4 \% \\ & 4+4=8 \\ & 850 \times 8 \%=68 \\ & 850+68 \times 3=1054 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#986
