mathedu,mathedu:0ef14dba327f9395,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Makes an arithmetic error when multiplying the cost factor by the profit factor,ok,\frac{16}{17} \times \frac{108}{100}  =\frac{402}{425}=0.95,ok,"the manager of a produce market purchased a quantity of tomatoes for $ 0.80 per pound . due to improper handling , 15 percent of the tomatoes , by weight , were ruined and discarded . at what price per pound should the manager sell the remaining tomatoes if she wishes to make a profit on the sale of the tomatoes equal to 8 percent of the cost of the tomatoes .",new cost of every tomatoes $$ \begin{aligned} & =\frac{0.8}{(1-15 \%)}=\frac{0.8}{0.85}=\frac{16}{17} \\ & \frac{16}{17} \times(1+8 \%) \\ & =\frac{16}{17} \times \frac{108}{100}  \\ & =\frac{402}{425}=0.95 \text { (dollars) } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#993
mathedu,mathedu:4c46598616a78766,,Careless error,Uses the wrong time interval to calculate speed,ok,The train needs 15 second to pass $750 \mathrm{~m}$,ok,a 750 m long train crosses a platform in 39 sec while it crosses a signal pole in 18 sec . what is the length of the platform ?,The train needs 15 second to pass $750 \mathrm{~m}$ So the speed is $750 \div 15=50 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec}$ 39 secund can pass $50 \times 39=1950 \mathrm{~m}$ $1950-750=1200 \mathrm{~m}$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#994
mathedu,mathedu:98b06622d0e50c11,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Divides the combined salary total by the number of workers unnecessarily,ok,1000 x=\frac{10 \cdot 1200+820(x-10)}{x},ok,"the average salary / head of all the workers in a workshop is rs . 1000 , if the average salary / head of 10 technician is rs . 1200 and the average salary / head of the rest is rs . 820 , the total no . of workers in the work - shop is ?",assume the total number of workers is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} & 1000 x=\frac{10 \cdot 1200+820(x-10)}{x} \\ & 1000 x^2=12000+820 x-8200 \\ & 1000 x^2-820 x-3800=0 \\ & 50 x^2-41 x-190=0 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1003
