mathedu,mathedu:291a291edf8df6e7,,Comprehension error,Equates accumulated amounts instead of equating the interest amounts,ok,(2691-x) \times(1+3 \% \times 8)=x \times(1+5 \% \times 3),ok,a sum of rs . 2691 is lent into two parts so that the interest on the first part for 8 years at 3 % per annum may be equal to the interest on the second part for 3 years at 5 % per annum . find the second sum ?,"assume the second sume $X$, then the first sum is $(2691-x)$ $$ \begin{aligned} & (2691-x) \times(1+3 \% \times 8)=x \times(1+5 \% \times 3) \\ & (2691-x) \times 1.24=1.15 x \\ & 2.39 x=2691 \times 1.24=3336.84 \\ & x=\frac{3336.84}{2.39} = 1396.17 \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1012
