mathedu,mathedu:d43699ef29b4c3d8,,Algebraic error,Treats interest values as total amounts instead of interest amounts,ok,x \times(1+i \times 2)=320,ok,"on a sum of money , the simple interest for 2 years is rs . 320 , while the compound interest is rs . 340 , the rate of interest being the same in both the cases . the rate of interest is","assume the principle $x$, interest $i$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array}{l} x \times(1+i \times 2)=320 \\ x \times(1+i)^2=340 \end{array}\right. \\ & \left\{\begin{array}{l} x+2 \times i=320 \\ x i^2+2 x i+x=340 \end{array}\right. \\ & x i^2=20 \\ & x+2 \times 20=320 \\ & x=280 \\ & l=\frac{40}{560} = 7.14 \%  \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1029
