mathedu,mathedu:e8f50f854b869e89,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats a percentage increase as the corresponding percentage decrease,ok,x \cdot(1-25 \%) \div \frac{1}{2}=8.50,ok,"at joes steakhouse the hourly wage for a chef is 25 % greater than that of a dishwasher , and the hourly wage of a dishwasher is half as much as the hourly wage of a manager . if a managers wage is $ 8.50 per hour , how much less than a manager does a chef earn each hour ?","Assume the chef can earn $\$ x$ per hour. $$ \begin{aligned} & x \cdot(1-25 \%) \div \frac{1}{2}=8.50 \\ & \Rightarrow 0.75 x \cdot 2=8.50 \\ & \Rightarrow 1,5 x=8.50 \\ & \Rightarrow x=\frac{8.5}{1.5}=\frac{17}{3} \\ & 8.50-\frac{17}{3}=\frac{17}{2}-\frac{17}{3}=\frac{51}{6}-\frac{34}{6}=\frac{17}{6} = 2.83 \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1051
