mathedu,mathedu:ad6897e5bf4ee29c,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Multiplies the percentage by the cost instead of equating it to the loss ratio,ok,\frac{\frac{2}{3} y-x}{x}=-0.25 x,ok,"what profit percent is made by selling an article at a certain price , if by selling at 2 / 3 rd of that price , there would be a loss of 25 % ?","assume the article's cost is $x$, certain price is $y$. $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{\frac{2}{3} y-x}{x}=-0.25 x \\ & \frac{2}{3} y-x=-0.25 x^2 \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1120
