mathedu,mathedu:d830e9f103a1f9fc,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Applies profit percentages directly instead of calculating them from cost prices,ok,\frac{21 \times 0.15+17 \times 0.25}{21+17}=0.194=19.4 \%,ok,"rani bought more apples than oranges . she sells apples at ₹ 23 apiece and makes 15 % profit . she sells oranges at ₹ 10 apiece and makes 25 % profit . if she gets ₹ 653 after selling all the apples and oranges , find her profit percentage z .","Apple: $x$ orange: $y$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 23 x+10 y=653, \quad x>y \\ & \Rightarrow x=11, y=40 \quad(\XSolid) \\ & x=21, y=17 \quad(Checkmark) \\ & \frac{21 \times 0.15+17 \times 0.25}{21+17}=0.194=19.4 \% \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1138
