mathedu,mathedu:c298c297c040c743,,Careless error,Computes the overtime rate using the hour threshold instead of the regular hourly rate,ok,[40 \times(1+75 \%)] \times(x-40),ok,"a certain bus driver is paid a regular rate of $ 16 per hour for any number of hours that does not exceed 40 hours per week . for any overtime hours worked in excess of 40 hours per week , the bus driver is paid a rate that is 75 % higher than his regular rate . if last week the bus driver earned $ 1200 in total compensation , how many total hours did he work that week ?",Assume he work $x$ hours. $$ \begin{aligned} & (16 \times 40)+[40 \times(1+75 \%)] \times(x-40)=1200 \\ & \Rightarrow 640+70(x-40)=1200 \\ & \Rightarrow 70 x-2800=560 \\ & \Rightarrow 70 x=3360 \\ & \Rightarrow x=48  \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1270
mathedu,mathedu:ff3e4b43a8044f48,,Comprehension error,Interprets a fixed amount more than twice as multiplication by that amount,ok,2(x+y)=8(4 x+2 y),ok,"in a group of ducks and cows , the total number of legs are 8 more than twice the no . of heads . find the total no . of buffaloes .","assume there are $x$ cows, $y$ ducks $$ \begin{aligned} & 2(x+y)=8(4 x+2 y) \\ & 2 x+2 y=32 x+16 y \\ & 30 x-14 y=0 \end{aligned} $$ Ans: there are more than one answer",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1272
