mathedu,mathedu:076eb970037c73d3,,Careless error,Uses an incorrect profit-share value in the calculation,ok,3600 \div \frac{24000+32000+36000}{36000},ok,"a , b and c started a partnership business by investing rs . 24000 , rs . 32000 , rs . 36000 respectively . at the end of the year , the profit were distributed among them . if c ' s share of profit is 36000 , what is the total profit ?",\begin{aligned} \text { total profit: } & 3600 \div \frac{24000+32000+36000}{36000} \\ & =3600 \div \frac{92}{36} \\ & =9200 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1295
mathedu,mathedu:39ec4a7a0c57b3b7,,Comprehension error,Reports the second quantity instead of the requested first quantity,ok,6 y=6000,ok,"the ratio of the incomes of rajan and balan is 7 : 6 and the ratio of their expenditure is 6 : 5 . if at the end of the year , each saves $ 1000 then the income of rajan is ?",income ratio = $7x:6x$ expenditure ratio = $6 y:5 y$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 7 x-6 y=1000 \\ & 6 x-5 y=1000 \\ & x-y=0 \\ & x=y=1000 \\ & 6 y=6000 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1297
mathedu,mathedu:d6b8934827bbf784,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats percentages of the remaining students as percentages of the total,ok,500 =x(100 \%-10 \%-20 \%-25 \%-24 \%-10 \%),ok,"in a practice paper at 2 iim . com , questions were given from 5 topics . out of the appearing students , 10 % passed in all topics while 10 % did not pass in any . of the remaining , 20 % passed in one topic only and 25 % in two topics only . if 24 % of the total students passed 4 topics only and 500 students passed in 3 topics only , find the total number of students who appeared in the examination ?",assume the total number of students is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} 500 & =x(100 \%-10 \%-20 \%-25 \%-24 \%-10 \%) \\ 500 & =0.11 x \\ x & =4545.45 \ldots . \end{aligned} $$ $\Rightarrow$ there are 4546 students in total.,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1298
