mathedu,mathedu:32ebfc960081b87a,,Comprehension error,Applies a percentage increase to the wrong base quantity,ok,1 \times\left(\frac{120}{100}+\frac{25}{100}\right),ok,"a particular store purchased a stock of turtleneck sweaters and marked up its cost by 20 % . during the new year season , it further marked up its prices by 25 % of the original retail price . in february , the store then offered a discount of 15 % . what was its profit on the items sold in february ?",\begin{aligned} & 1 \times\left(\frac{120}{100}+\frac{25}{100}\right) \times \frac{85}{100} \\ = & \frac{145}{100} \times \frac{85}{100} \\ = & \frac{493}{400} \\ & \frac{493}{400}-1=\frac{93}{400} \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1353
