mathedu,mathedu:89f9865d4fced483,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Assumes the minimum occurs at an endpoint without checking interior points,ok,if x is p ... xz=5 cm,ok,"in triangle pqr , the angle q = 90 degree , pq = 5 cm , qr = 8 cm . x is a variable point on pq . the line through x parallel to qr , intersects pr at y and the line through y , parallel to pq , intersects qr at z . find the least possible length of xz",\begin{aligned} & \text { if } x \text { is } p \\ \Rightarrow & y \text { is } p \\ \Rightarrow & z \text { is } q \\ \Rightarrow & \overline{x z}=5 \mathrm{~cm} \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1365
