mathedu,mathedu:2bf965a002bfc822,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Fails to double the individual-purchase amount for two people,ok,243-117 = 126,ok,"huey ' s hip pizza sells two sizes of square pizzas : a small pizza that measures 6 inches on a side and costs $ 10 , and a large pizza that measures 9 inches on a side and costs $ 20 . if two friends go to huey ' s with $ 30 apiece , how many more square inches of pizza can they buy if they pool their money than if they each purchase pizza alone ?",$$ \begin{aligned} & 6 \times 6=36 \\ & 9 \times 9=81 \end{aligned} $$ a person can buy $$ 36+81=117 $$ two people can buy $$ 81 \times 3=243 \\ 243-117 = 126 $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1382
mathedu,mathedu:c8a0799c0b298912,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Incorrectly cross-multiplies fractions involving variable denominators,ok,4 x y=3 x y+360 y,ok,"in a covering a certain distance , the speeds of a and b are in the ratio of 3 : 4 . a takes 30 minutes more than b to reach the destination . the time taken by a to reach the destination is ?",$$ a:b=3: 4=3 y:4 y \quad(y>0) $$ assume the distance $X \mathrm{~km}$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{x}{3 y}=\frac{x}{4 y}+30 \\ & 4 x y=3 x y+360 y \\ & x y=360 y \quad x=360 \\ & \text { request: } \frac{x}{4 y}=\frac{360}{4 y} \\ & 1440 y=1080 y+360 y \end{aligned} $$ y can be any number $\Rightarrow$ more than one answers,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1395
