mathedu,mathedu:1dff56baaf3387b8,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Reports average speed using distance units instead of speed units,ok,=8+16=24\ \mathrm{~km},ok,a trained covered x km at 40 kmph and another 2 x km at 20 kmph . find the average speed of the train in covering the entire 6 x km .,$40 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} \rightarrow 2 x$ distance $20 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} \rightarrow 4 x$ distance Assume $x=40$ $$ \begin{aligned} 40 \times 2 & =80 \mathrm{~km} \\ 40 \times 4 & =160 \mathrm{~km} \end{aligned} $$ $80 \mathrm{~km} \div 40=2$ $160 \mathrm{~km} \div 20=8$ $2+8=10 \Rightarrow$ total travel hours $$ \frac{2}{10} \times 40+\frac{8}{10} \times 20=8+16=24 \mathrm{~km}  $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1464
mathedu,mathedu:febc0a6d99996d1a,,Comprehension error,Uses the changed rate instead of the original rate for the actual distance,ok,7 \times 10=70 \mathrm{~km},ok,"if a person walks at 10 km / hr instead of 8 km / hr , he would have walked 14 km more . the actual distance traveled by him is ?",\begin{aligned} & 14 \div(10-8)=7 \\ & 7 \times 10=70 \mathrm{~km} \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1465
mathedu,mathedu:69892951c49526ab,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Subtracts the tax rate instead of dividing by one plus the tax rate,ok,40 \times \frac{3}{10} \times\left(1-\frac{6}{100}\right),ok,"jerry went to a shop and bought things worth rs . 40 , out of which 30 % went on sales tax on taxable purchases . if the tax rate was 6 % , then what was the cost of the tax free items ?",\begin{aligned} & 40 \times \frac{3}{10} \times\left(1-\frac{6}{100}\right) \\ = & 12 \times \frac{94}{100} \\ = & 11.28 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1473
