mathedu,mathedu:9115aabc9a51c37b,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats each removed mixture volume as an equal amount of pure component,ok,\frac{36-2 x}{100}=\frac{16}{100},ok,"a 100 - litre mixture of milk and water contains 36 litres of milk . ' x ' litres of this mixture is removed and replaced with an equal quantum of water . if the process is repeated once , then the concentration of the milk stands reduced at 16 % . what is the value of x ?",\begin{aligned} & \frac{36-2 x}{100}=\frac{16}{100} \\ & 36-2 x=16 \\ & x=10 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1481
mathedu,mathedu:8f89cfe4e6c7b3fc,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Applies count ratios directly to a total value instead of converting value to counts,ok,75000 \div 3=25000,ok,"a certain scholarship committee awarded scholarships in the amounts of $ 1250 , $ 2500 and $ 4000 . the committee awarded twice as many $ 2500 scholarships as $ 4000 and it awarded 3 times as many $ 1250 scholarships as $ 2500 scholarships . if the total of $ 75000 was awarded in $ 1250 scholarships , how many $ 4000 scholarships were awarded ?",\begin{aligned} & 75000 \div 3=25000 \\ & 25000 \div 2=12500 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1484
mathedu,mathedu:2e082d60db84b47b,,Careless error,Uses the solved time as a scaling factor instead of the quantity ratio,ok,(t+2) \times 4=6 \times 4=24,ok,"machine r takes 2 more hours than machine b to make 20 widgets . if working together , the machines can make 25 widgets in 3 hours , how long will it take machine r to make 40 widgets ?","t is time for machine $b$ to make 20 widgets. $(t+2) \times 2$ is time for machine $r$ to make 40 widgets $$ \begin{aligned} & 3 \times\left(\frac{20}{t}+\frac{20}{t+2}\right)=25 \\ & 25 t^2+50 t=120 t+120 \\ & 5 t^2-14 t-24=0 \\ & t=-\frac{6}{5}, 4 \\ & (t+2) \times 4=6 \times 4=24 \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1517
