mathedu,mathedu:ebda933512058ee9,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats “more than twice” as fixed values instead of an additive equation,ok,x+y=\frac { 1 } { 2 } \times 1 6 \\ ... \\ 4 x + 2 y = 1 6,ok,"in a group of cows and chickens , the number of legs was 16 more than twice the number of heads . the number of cows was :","assume there are $x$ cows and y chickens. $$ \begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array} { l }  { x + y = \frac { 1 } { 2 } \times 1 6 } \\ { 4 x + 2 y = 1 6 } \end{array} \Rightarrow \left\{\begin{array}{l} x+y=8 \ldots(1) \\ 2 x+y=8 \ldots(2) \end{array}\right.\right. \\ & (2)-(1), x=0 \Rightarrow y=8 \end{aligned} $$ $\therefore$ there are no cows. ",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1647
