mathedu,mathedu:3234bfd940abbda5,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Omits the factor of two in the rectangle’s perimeter formula,ok,\frac{8 \times 200}{3+2}=\frac{1600}{5}=320,ok,"a man cycles round the boundary of a rectangular park at the rate of 12 kmph and completes one full round in 8 minutes . if the ratio between the length and breadth of the park be 3 : 2 , then its area is :",$$ \begin{aligned} & 12 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr}=12000 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{hr}=200 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{min} \\ & \frac{8 \times 200}{3+2}=\frac{1600}{5}=320 \\ & (3 \times 320)(2 \times 320)=960 \times 640=614400\left(\mathrm{~m}^2\right) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1662
