mathedu,mathedu:85291a9fbc75f201,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Makes an arithmetic error when solving the resulting linear equation,ok,5 x =140-35 \\ x & =23,ok,there are 2 friends peter and paul . peter age is twice as old as paul when peter was as old as paul is now . sum of the present ages of peter and paul is 35 . what is the present age of peter ?,assume peter is $x$ years old now. $$ \begin{aligned} & \text { present age of }\left\{\begin{array}{l} \text { peter : } x \\ \text { paul : } 35-x \end{array}\right. \\ & \begin{aligned} 35-x & =2[(35-x)+(35-x)-x] \\ 35-x & =2(70-3 x) \\ 5 x & =140-35 \\ x & =23 \text { (years old) } \end{aligned} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1694
mathedu,mathedu:a6dd83393b2a6e35,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Confuses the combined work rate with an individual worker’s rate,ok,arum's \& tarum's speed $=\frac{1}{10}$ per day ... $\frac{1-\frac{4}{5}}{\frac{1}{10}}$,ok,arun and tarun can do a work in 10 days . after 4 days tarun went to his village . how many days are required to complete the remaining work by arun alone . arun can do the work alone in 20 days .,arum's \& tarum's speed $=\frac{1}{10}$ per day $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{1}{10} \times 2 \times 4=\frac{4}{5} \\ & \frac{1-\frac{4}{5}}{\frac{1}{10}}=\frac{\frac{1}{5}}{\frac{1}{10}}=2(\text { days }) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1697
