mathedu,mathedu:9260573332452c45,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Adds overlapping counts as though they represent disjoint categories,ok,(1-20 \%-10 \%) \times x=22+32,ok,"of the diplomats attending a summit conference , 22 speak french , 32 do not speak russian , and 20 % of the diplomats speak neither french nor russian . if 10 % of the diplomats speak both languages , then how many diplomats attended the conference ?",Assure there are $x$ diplomats. $$ \begin{aligned} & (1-20 \%-10 \%) \times x=22+32 \\ & 70 \% x=54 \\ & x = 77 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1714
mathedu,mathedu:37ca5c005892f048,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses the wrong duration when calculating a rate's contribution,ok,\frac{1}{14} \times 1.5+x=\frac{1}{2},ok,"one pump drains one - half of a pond in 7 hours , and then a second pump starts draining the pond . the two pumps working together finish emptying the pond in one - half hour . how long would it take the second pump to drain the pond if it had to do the job alone ?",first bump: $\frac{1}{7} \times \frac{1}{2}=\frac{1}{14}$ per hour assume the second bump's speed $=x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{1}{14} \times 1.5+x=\frac{1}{2} \\ & x=\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{14} \times \frac{3}{2} \\ & =\frac{14-3}{28}=\frac{11}{28} \\ & \frac{1}{x}=\frac{28}{11} =2.54 \mathrm{hr} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1715
mathedu,mathedu:142841532bc9868a,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Omits the cone’s height when calculating its volume,ok,\frac{1}{3}\left(x^2 \pi\right),ok,"a cylindrical container of radius 6 cm and height 15 cm is filled with ice - cream . the whole icecream has to be distributed to 10 children in equal cones with hemispherical tops . if the height of the conical portion is four times the radius of its base , find the radius of the ice - cream cone .",assume the radius of the ice-cream cone is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} 6^2 \times 15 \pi & =10\left[\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{4}{3} \pi x^3\right)+\frac{1}{3}\left(x^2 \pi\right)\right] \\ 540 \pi & =10\left(\frac{2}{3} \pi x^3+\frac{1}{3} \pi x^2\right) \\ 54 \pi & =\pi\left(\frac{2}{3} x^3+\frac{1}{3} x^2\right) \\ 162 & =2 x^3+x^2 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1717
mathedu,mathedu:472a37b82edc8a14,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses water percentages instead of complementary conserved-material percentages,ok,5 \div 20 \% =5 \div 0.2 =25,ok,"if grapes are 92 % water and raisins are 20 % water , then how many kilograms did a quantity of raisins , which currently weighs 5 kilograms , weigh when all the raisins were grapes ? ( assume that the only difference between their raisin - weight and their grape - weight is water that evaporated during their transformation . )",\begin{aligned} & 5 \div 20 \% \\ & =5 \div 0.2 \\ & =25 \\ & 25 \times 92 \% \\ & =25 \times 0.92 \\ & =23 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1718
mathedu,mathedu:94dd495e1b43f6cc,,Comprehension error,Sets total legs equal to the stated excess instead of adding it to twice the heads,ok,4 x+2 y=20,ok,"in a group of cows and chickens , the number of legs was 20 more than twice the number of heads . the number of cows was :",cows: $x$ chicken : Y $$ \begin{aligned} & 4 x+2 y=20 \\ & x+y=\frac{20}{2}=10 \\ & 2 x+2 y=20 \\ & 2 x=0 \\ & x=0 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1736
