mathedu,mathedu:4875c35686ba0eec,,Unfinished answer,Confuses the range with the interval from minimum to maximum,ok,range $=2$ to 19,ok,"tough and tricky questions : statistics . set x consists of prime numbers { 3 , 11 , 7 , a , 17 , 19 } . if integer y represents the product of all elements in set x and if 11 y is an even number , what is the range of set x ?","$$ \begin{aligned} & y=3 \times 11 \times 7 \times a \times 17 \times 19 \\ & 11 y=2 \alpha \\ & 11y=3 \times 11^2 \times 7 \times a \times 17 \times 19=2 \alpha\right. \end{aligned} $$ $\therefore$ a must be a multiple of 2 , should be a prime number $\Rightarrow a=2$ range $=2$ to 19",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1749
