mathedu,mathedu:471fa67ddc91983e,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Misinterprets a half-efficiency relationship as a three-halves rate ratio,ok,18 r \geq\left(r+\frac{3}{2} r\right),ok,"ram , who is half as efficient as krish , will take 18 days to complete a task if he worked alone . if ram and krish worked together , how long will they take to complete the task ?",\begin{aligned} & 18 r \geq\left(r+\frac{3}{2} r\right) \\ = & 18 r \geq \frac{5}{2} r \\ = & 18 \times \frac{2}{5}=\frac{36}{5}=7.2 \mathrm{days} \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1762
