mathedu,mathedu:fa0dbbe868114463,,Unfinished answer,Fails to convert the reduced running distance into the head-start distance,ok,Ans $=b$ only need to run $\frac{15}{17}$ of total length,ok,"a ’ s speed is 17 / 15 times that of b . if a and b run a race , what part of the length of the race should a give b as a head start , so that the race ends in a dead heat ?","assume $a^{\prime}$ s speed $a$, then b's speed $\frac{15}{17} a$ assume the total length X a's time $=\frac{x}{a}=b^{\prime}$ s time ,b's length $=\frac{x}{a} \times \frac{15}{17} a x=\frac{15}{17} x$ Ans $=b$ only need to run $\frac{15}{17}$ of total length",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1785
