mathedu,mathedu:b214500c780da5f8,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats the HCF as a sum rather than a common factor,ok,h+F=18,ok,the h . c . f . of two numbers is 18 and the other two factors of their l . c . m . are 11 and 15 . the larger of the two numbers is :,$$ \left\{\begin{array}{l} h+F=18 - (1) \\ h F=I-(2) \end{array}\right. $$ the factors of $I$ are 11 and 15 $$ \begin{aligned} & 11 \times 15=165=I \\ & h+F=18 \\ & \Rightarrow h=18-F \end{aligned} $$ put $h=18-F$ into (2) $$ \begin{aligned} & \Rightarrow(18-F) F=165 \\ & \Rightarrow F^2-18 F+165=0 \end{aligned} $$ Use formula: $\frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2-4 a c}}{2 a}$ $\Rightarrow \frac{18 \pm \sqrt{324-660}}{2} \Rightarrow$ no answer,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1796
