mathedu,mathedu:0bfa5a44571d4f81,,Arithmetical error,Rounds a fractional time up to the next whole number unnecessarily,ok,3+1=4,ok,a money lender lent rs . 1000 at 4 % per year and rs . 1400 at 5 % per year . the amount should be returned to him when the total interest comes to rs . 350 . find the number of years .,Interest per year is $1000 \times 4 \%+1400 \times 5 \%=110$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 350 \div 110 = 3.18 \\ & 3+1=4 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1856
mathedu,mathedu:66c22c60f441f55c,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Reports the non-upgraded fraction as the upgraded fraction,ok,\frac{6 y-y}{6 y}=\frac{5}{6},ok,"a satellite is composed of 30 modular units , each of which is equipped with a set of sensors , some of which have been upgraded . each unit contains the same number of non - upgraded sensors . if the number of non - upgraded sensors on one unit is 1 / 6 the total number of upgraded sensors on the entire satellite , what fraction of the sensors on the satellite have been upgraded ?","Assume each unit have $x$ sensors, in which $y$, is upgraded $$ \begin{aligned} & x-y=30 y \times \frac{1}{6} \\ & x-y=5 y \\ & x=6 y \\ & \frac{6 y-y}{6 y}=\frac{5}{6} \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1861
mathedu,mathedu:2091be3e5f32eecc,,Algebraic error,Incorrectly simplifies the difference of fractional coefficients,ok,\frac{10}{15} x=1200,ok,"mary and mike enter into a partnership by investing $ 800 and $ 200 respectively . at the end of one year , they divided their profits such that a third of the profit is divided equally for the efforts they have put into the business and the remaining amount of profit is divided in the ratio of the investments they made in the business . if mary received $ 1200 more than mike did , what was the profit made by their business in that year ?",assume the profit e of the year $x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \text { Mary and Mike's initial investment }=800: 200 \\ & =4:1 \\ & \text { Mary: } \frac{1}{3} x \times \frac{1}{2}+\frac{2}{3} x \times \frac{4}{5} \\ & \text { Mike }=\frac{1}{3} x \times \frac{1}{2}+\frac{2}{3} x \times \frac{1}{5} \\ & \Rightarrow\left(\frac{1}{6} x+\frac{8}{15} x\right)-\left(\frac{1}{6} x+\frac{2}{15} x\right)=1200 \\ & \frac{10}{15} x=1200 \\ & x=120 \times 15=1800 \text { (dollars) } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1876
mathedu,mathedu:dec346119589f710,,Unfinished answer,Reports the ratio in reverse order,ok,x: y=3: 8,ok,"a boat running upstream takes 8 hours 48 minutes to cover a certain distance , while it takes 4 hours to cover the same distance running downstream . what is the ratio between the speed of the boat and speed of the water current respectively ?","Assume the speed of water is $X \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr}$, boat is $$ \begin{aligned} & y \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} . \\ & (y-x) \cdot \frac{528}{60}=(y+x) \cdot \frac{240}{60} \\ \Rightarrow & (y-x) \cdot 528=(y+x) \cdot 240 \\ \Rightarrow & 528 y-528 x=240 y+240 x \\ \Rightarrow & 288 y=768 x \\ \Rightarrow & 96 y=256 x \\ \Rightarrow & 24 y=64 x \\ \Rightarrow & 3 y=8 x \\ \Rightarrow & x: y=3: 8 \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1883
