mathedu,mathedu:689ab1a0018c208d,,Lack of necessary mathematical concepts,Misinterprets doubling the number as doubling the divisor,ok,& x \bmod 2 y=112,ok,"a number when divided by a certain divisor left remainder 251 , when twice the number was divided by the same divisor , the remainder was 112 . find the divisor ?","Assume the number is $x$, divisor is $y$ $$ \begin{aligned} & x \bmod y=251 \\ & x \bmod 2 y=112 \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1893
mathedu,mathedu:dd2efa172436b8d8,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses the total population instead of restricting the denominator to college graduates,ok,the probability $=\frac{x}{x+8 x+12 x+3 x}=\frac{1}{24}$,ok,"in a certain large company , the ratio of college graduates with a graduate degree to non - college graduates is 1 : 8 , and ratio of college graduates without a graduate degree to non - college graduates is 2 : 3 . if one picks a random college graduate at this large company , what is the probability w this college graduate has a graduate degree ?",1229 \begin{tabular}{l|c|c}  & $\begin{array}{l}\text { graduate } \\ \text { degree } V\end{array}$ & $\begin{array}{l}\text { graduate } \\ \text { degree X }\end{array}$ \\ \hline $\begin{array}{l}\text { college } \\ \text { graduate } V\end{array}$ & $X$ & $2 x$ \\ \hline $\begin{array}{l}\text { college } \\ \text { graduate } X\end{array}$ & $8 x$ & $3 x$ \end{tabular} the probability $=\frac{x}{x+8 x+12 x+3 x}=\frac{1}{24}$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1895
mathedu,mathedu:87b586fd987f6e69,,Comprehension error,Reverses which hourly rate is $35 higher,ok,x+(x+35)+(x+35+35)+(x+35 \times 3)+(x+35 \times 4)=350,ok,"a certain psychologist charges $ 35 more for the first hour of therapy than for each additional hour . if the total charge to a patient who receives 5 hours of therapy is $ 350 , what is the total charge to a patient who receives only 2 hours of therapy ?",Assume the first hour cost $x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & x+(x+35)+(x+35+35)+(x+35 \times 3)+(x+35 \times 4)=350 \\ & 5 x+35 \times 10=350 \\ & 5 x=0 \\ & x=0 \end{aligned} $$ So the total charge for 2 hours therapy will be $ 0+0+35=35$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1904
