mathedu,mathedu:16ef17cf74033419,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses multiplication by two instead of squaring,ok,(5 \times 2+14) \div 12=2 \ldots 0,ok,"if p is a prime number greater than 3 , find the remainder when p ^ 2 + 14 is divided by 12 .",if $p=5:(5 \times 2+14) \div 12=2 \ldots 0$ if $p=7:(7 \times 2+14) \div 12=2 \ldots 4$ if $p=11:(11 \times 2+14) \div 12=3 \ldots 0  if $p=13:(13 \times 2+14) \div 12=3 \ldots 4$  if $p=17:(17 \times 2+14) \div 12=4 \ldots 0$ \\ \Rightarrow$ the remainder may be 0 or 4,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1910
mathedu,mathedu:31420831412e28b8,,Comprehension error,Uses the prior count instead of the updated count for the target average,ok,11 × 19 − (14 × 11 + 26) = 209 − 180 = 29,ok,a batsman scores 26 runs and increases his average from 14 to 15 . find the runs to be made if he wants top increasing the average to 19 in the same match ?,assume $x$ rounds of play have been played. $$ \begin{aligned} & 14 x+26=15(x+1) \\ & x=26-15=11 \\ & 11 \times 19-(14 \times 11+26)=209-180=29 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1912
