mathedu,mathedu:f0a19755c7d87d8b,,Algebraic error,Divides by the wrong coefficient when solving a linear equation,ok,6 x = 1342.86-940 \quad & \ & x=\frac{402.86}{4},ok,"a reduction of 30 % in the price of oil enables a house wife to obtain 6 kgs more for rs . 940 , what is the reduced price for kg ?",assume the original oil price $x$ rs. $/ \mathrm{kg}$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{940}{x}+6=\frac{940}{0.7 x} \\ & 940+6 x=\frac{940}{0.7} \\ & 6 x = 1342.86-940 \\ & x=\frac{402.86}{4} \\ & = 100.72 \\ & \text { reduced price }=100.72 \times 0.7= 70.5 \mathrm{rs} / \mathrm{kg} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1941
