mathedu,mathedu:64a904e1ed9c4e1a,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats a rate of items per currency as a per-item monetary price,ok,\frac{x-8}{8}=5 \%,ok,if a man lost 5 % by selling oranges at the rate of 8 a rupee at how many a rupee must he sell them to gain 52 % ?,assume the cost of a orange $x$ rs. $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{x-8}{8}=5 \% \\ & x-8=0.4 \\ & x=8.4 \end{aligned} $$ selling price set as $y$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{y-8.4}{y}=52 \% \\ & 0.48 y=8.4 \quad y=8.4 \times \frac{100}{48}=17.5(rs) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1972
mathedu,mathedu:48ccfc1cc935f2e9,,Arithmetical error,Makes an arithmetic error when multiplying the final quantities,ok,$11.25 \times 8=89$ liters,ok,"45 litres of diesel is required to travel 600 km using a 800 cc engine . if the volume of diesel required to cover a distance varies directly as the capacity of the engine , then how many litres of diesel is required to travel 800 km using 1200 cc engine ?",$800 \mathrm{cc}$ engine need $45 \div 6=7.5$ liters for  $100 \mathrm{~km}$ $1200 \mathrm{CC}$ engine need $7.5 \times \frac{1200}{800}=11.25$ liters for $100 \mathrm{~km}$ $11.25 \times 8=89$ liters,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#1974
