mathedu,mathedu:30dea61f3d9f8798,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Reverses the meaning of “twice” in the relationship,ok,x=2 y+74 \ldots \text { (2) },ok,"joan and karl each bought a telescopes and the sum of their purchases was $ 400 . if twice of what joan paid was $ 74 more than what karl paid , what did joan pay for her telescope ?","assume joan's telescope is $\$ x$, and karl's telescope is $\$ y$. $$ \left\{\begin{array}{l} x+y=400 \ldots \text { (1) } \\ x=2 y+74 \ldots \text { (2) } \end{array}\right. $$ substitute $400-x$ for $y$ in (2) $$ \begin{aligned} \Rightarrow \quad x & =2(400-x)+74 \\ x & =800-2 x+74 \\ 3 x & =874 \\ x & =291 \frac{1}{3} \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2099
