mathedu,mathedu:bbcddf9d32a47e75,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Assumes the relevant points bisect the dimensions without justification,ok,20 \div 2=10 \quad 25 \div 2=12: 5,ok,"the rhombus ( afce ) is inscribed in rectangle ( abcd ) . the length of bf = de . if the rectangle has a width of 20 yards and a length of 25 yards , what would be the total length ( the perimeter ) of a fence along the sides defined by afce ?",\begin{aligned} & 20 \div 2=10 \\ & 25 \div 2=12: 5 \\ & \sqrt{10^2+12.5^2} = 16 \\ & 16 \times 4=64 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2109
