mathedu,mathedu:3dd6a547139afcea,,Algebraic error,Infers a variable ratio from a single linear equation,ok,-4 x+15 y =2 \quad \frac{x}{y} \mid \frac{1}{2},ok,"a man covered a certain distance at some speed . had he moved 3 kmph faster , he would have taken 40 minutes less . if he had moved 2 kmph slower , he would have taken 40 minutes more . the distance ( in km ) is","assume man's original speed is $x(\mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr})$, and he spend $y$ hours. $$ \begin{aligned} & 40 \text { min }=\frac{2}{3} \text { hrs } \\ & \left\{\begin{array} { l }  { \frac { x y } { x + 3 } = y - \frac { 2 } { 3 } } \\ { \frac { x y } { x - 2 } = y + \frac { 2 } { 3 } } \end{array} \Rightarrow \left\{\begin{array}{l} x y=(x+3)\left(y-\frac{2}{3}\right) \ldots \text { (1) } \\ x y=(x-2)\left(y+\frac{2}{3}\right) \ldots \text { (2) } \end{array}\right.\right. \end{aligned} $$ $\operatorname{mix}(1) \&$ (2) $$ \begin{aligned} \Rightarrow(x+3)\left(y-\frac{2}{3}\right) & =(x-2)\left(y+\frac{2}{3}\right) \\ x y-\frac{2}{3} x+3 y-2 & =x y+\frac{2}{3} x-2 y-\frac{4}{3} \\ -\frac{4}{3} x+5 y & =\frac{2}{3} \\ -4 x+15 y & =2 \quad \frac{x}{y} \mid \frac{1}{2} \end{aligned} $$ $\therefore$ the distance $=7 \times 2=14(\mathrm{~km}) $",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2127
