mathedu,mathedu:794213ba290880d0,,Comprehension error,Counts non-operating days as operating days,ok,14-3=11 \Rightarrow$ not hot day.,ok,"sarah operated her lemonade stand monday through friday over a two week period and made a total profit of 350 dollars . on hot days she sold cups of lemonade for a price that was 25 percent higher than the regular days . each cup she sold had a total cost of 75 cents and sarah did not incur any other costs . if every day she sold exactly 32 cups and 3 of the days were hot , then what was the price of 1 cup on a hot day ?",Assume normal price is $x$ dollars. 14-3=11 \Rightarrow$ not hot day. 75 cents $=0.75$ dollars. $$ \begin{aligned} & 32 .(x-0.75) \times 11+32 .(1.25 x-0.73) \times 3=350 \\ & \Rightarrow(32 x-24) \times 11+(40 x-24) \times 3=350 \\ & \Rightarrow 352 x+120 x-264-72=350 \\ & \Rightarrow 472 x=350+336=686 \\ & \Rightarrow x=686 \div 472 \fallingdotseq 1.45 \text { dollars } \\ & (1.45) \times(1.25)=1.8125 \text { dollars }  \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2216
mathedu,mathedu:2bf6ae8c005617d7,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses selling price instead of cost price as the profit percentage denominator,ok,\frac{(1-5 \%) x-y}{(1-5 \%) x}=25 \%,ok,a shopkeeper sold an book offering a discount of 5 % and earned a profit of 25 % . what would have been the percentage of profit earned if no discount was offered ?,"assume the original selling price x, cost y$$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{(1-5 \%) x-y}{(1-5 \%) x}=25 \% \\ & 0.95 x-y=0.95 \times 0.25=0.2375 x \\ & 0.7165 x=y \\ & \frac{x-y}{x}=1-\frac{y}{x}=1-0.7165 \\ & =28.35 \% \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2219
