mathedu,mathedu:896c76fc61a61b9b,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Calculates the target percentage from an incomplete original total,ok,{[(4 x \cdot 0.25)-0.25 x-0.5 x] \div 2},ok,"a bowl contains equal numbers of red , orange , green , blue , and yellow candies . kaz eats all of the green candies and half of the orange ones . next , he eats half of the remaining pieces of each color . finally , he eats red and yellow candies in equal proportions until the total number of remaining candies of all colors equals 25 % of the original number . what percent of the red candies remain ?",Assume the number of red candies is $x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & {[(4 x \cdot 0.25)-0.25 x-0.5 x] \div 2} \\ & =(x-0.75 x) \div 2 \\ & =0.125 x \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2306
mathedu,mathedu:563a7de2ad38766c,,Arithmetical error,Makes an arithmetic error when dividing distance by relative speed,ok,75 \div \frac{20}{3} =500 \text { seconds. },ok,a bus 75 m long is running with a speed of 21 km / hr . in what time will it pass a woman who is walking at 3 km / hr in the direction opposite to that in which the bus is going ?,$21+3=24 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} \Rightarrow$ the decrease of distance between the bus \& woman. $$ \begin{aligned} & 24 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} \\ & =(2400 \div 60 \div 60) \mathrm{m} / \mathrm{sec} \\ & =\frac{20}{3} \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec} \\ & 75 \div \frac{20}{3} \\ & =500 \text { seconds. } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2311
