mathedu,mathedu:d9c84f0e31803f1e,,Careless error,Uses twice a variable’s value when substituting into an equation,ok,substitute 20 for $y$ in 1 (1) $\Rightarrow x+40=44$,ok,"a man has some hens and cows . if the number of heads be 44 and the number of feet equals 128 , then the number of hens will be",assume there are $x$ hens \& $y$ cows. $$ \begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array} { l }  { x + y = 4 4 } \\ { 2 x + 4 y = 1 2 8 } \end{array} \Rightarrow \left\{\begin{array}{l} x+y=44 \ldots \text { (1) } \\ x+2 y=64 \ldots \text { (8) } \end{array}\right.\right. \\ & \text { (3)-(1) } \Rightarrow y=20 \end{aligned} $$ substitute 20 for $y$ in 1 (1) $\Rightarrow x+40=44$ $$ x=4 $$ $\therefore$ the man has 4 hens.,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2361
mathedu,mathedu:7bfa6f3db152fcd0,,Unfinished answer,Fails to convert the calculated time into the requested units,ok,=1.25 \text { hours },ok,"cole drove from home to work at an average speed of 60 kmh . he then returned home at an average speed of 100 kmh . if the round trip took a total of 2 hours , how many minutes did it take cole to drive to work ?",Assume the distance is $x \mathrm{~km}$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{x}{60}+\frac{x}{100}=2 \mathrm{hr} . \\ & \Rightarrow \frac{8 x}{300}=2 \\ & \Rightarrow 8 x=600 \\ & \Rightarrow x=600 \div 8=75 \\ & 75 \mathrm{~km} \div 60 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr}=\frac{75}{60}=\frac{5}{4}=1.25 \text { hours } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2365
