mathedu,mathedu:3575bb04215b5240,,Comprehension error,Misreads a mixed-number value as its whole-number part,ok,$7+1.5=8.5 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr}$,ok,"a man can row 7 â ½ kmph in still water . if in a river running at 1.5 km / hr an hour , it takes him 50 minutes to row to a place and back , how far off is the place ?",$7+1.5=8.5 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} \Rightarrow$ row with current $7-1.5=5.5 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{mm} \Rightarrow$ row against current Assume the distance is $X \mathrm{~km}$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{x}{8.5}+\frac{x}{5.5}=\frac{50}{60} \text { hour } \\ & \Rightarrow \frac{11 x}{93.5}+\frac{17 x}{93.5}=\frac{5}{6} \\ & \Rightarrow \frac{28 x}{93.5}=\frac{5}{6} \\ & \Rightarrow x=\frac{5}{6} \div \frac{28}{93.5}=\frac{467.5}{168}=\frac{935}{336} \mathrm{~km} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2406
mathedu,mathedu:131b9e0b6a8bd3ea,,Comprehension error,Confuses half the total time with half the tank's volume,ok,\frac{\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{1}{40}}+\frac{\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{1}{60}+\frac{1}{40}},ok,a tank can be filled by two pipes a and b in 60 minutes and 40 minutes respectively . how many minutes will it take to fill the tank from empty state if b is used for the first half time and then a and b fill it together for the other half,"the speed of $a=\frac{1}{60}, b=\frac{1}{40}$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{1}{40}}+\frac{\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{1}{60}+\frac{1}{40}} \\ = & 20+\frac{\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{5}{120}} \\ = & 32(\mathrm{~min}) \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2410
mathedu,mathedu:aa0051173b826a29,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Incorrectly sets separate factors equal when only their product is specified,ok,\left\{\begin{array}{l} 4^a \times 5^b \times 7^{(n-a-b)}=175 \\ \left(\frac{1}{10}\right)^n=\frac{1}{100000} \end{array}\right.,ok,"an army ’ s recruitment process included n rounds of selection tasks . for the first a rounds , the rejection percentage was 60 percent per round . for the next b rounds , the rejection percentage was 50 percent per round and for the remaining rounds , the selection percentage was 70 percent per round . if there were 100000 people who applied for the army and 175 were finally selected , what was the value of n ?",\begin{aligned} & 100000 \times\left[(1-60 \%)^a\right] \times\left[(1-50 \%)^b\right] \times \\ & {\left[(70 \%)^{(n-a-b)}\right]=175} \\ & \Rightarrow(0.4)^a(0.5)^b(0.7)^{(n-a-b)}=\frac{175}{100000} \\ & \Rightarrow\left(\frac{1}{10}\right)^{(a+b+n-a-b)}(4)^a(5)^b(7)^{(n-a -b)}=\frac{175}{100000} \\ & \Rightarrow\left\{\begin{array}{l} 4^a \times 5^b \times 7^{(n-a-b)}=175 \\ \left(\frac{1}{10}\right)^{(a+b+n-a-b)}=\left(\frac{1}{10}\right)^n=\frac{1}{100000} \end{array}\right. \\ & \Rightarrow n=5 \\ & \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2412
mathedu,mathedu:595b64cd678cefde,,Comprehension error,Uses area ratio instead of perimeter ratio to scale time for one round,ok,18 x^2 \div 1.5 x^2=12 \quad 20 \times 12=240,ok,if a person has two rectangular fields . the larger field has thrice the length and 4 times the width of the smaller field . if the smaller field has a length 50 % more than the width . if a person takes 20 minutes to complete one round of a smaller field then what is the time required to complete one round of a larger field ?,Assume the width of the smaller field is $x$ the length of the smaller field is $1.5 x$ the length of the larger field is $4.5 x$ the with of the larger field is $4 X$ the area of the smaller field $$ \Rightarrow x \cdot 1.5 x=1.5 x^2 $$ the area of the larger field $$ \begin{aligned} & \Rightarrow 4.5 x \cdot 4 x=18 x^2 \\ & 18 x^2 \div 1.5 x^2=12 \\ & 20 \times 12=240 \text { miss }  \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2423
mathedu,mathedu:5641a39689dbcfec,,Measurement error,Fails to convert area units into corresponding length units,ok,the diagonal of the square is $\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}} \times \sqrt{2}=1$,ok,area of a square is 1 / 2 hectare . the diagonal of the square is ?,the side length of the square is $\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}}$ the diagonal of the square is $\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}} \times \sqrt{2}=1$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2425
mathedu,mathedu:9f9fbc5b93a0dc38,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Replaces squared terms with linear terms when expanding the defined operation,ok,100 =8 a+8 b+8 a b,ok,"tough and tricky questions : word problems . operation # is defined as : a # b = 4 a ^ 2 + 4 b ^ 2 + 8 ab for all non - negative integers . what is the value of ( a + b ) + 8 , when a # b = 100 ?",\begin{aligned} a \# b & =4 a^{\wedge} 2+4 b^{\wedge} 2+8 a b \\ 100 & =8 a+8 b+8 a b \\ 100 & =8(a+b)+8 a b \\ 8(a+b) & =100-8 a b \\ a+b & =\frac{100-8 a b}{8} \\ a+b & =\frac{25-2 a b}{2} \\ \therefore(a+b)+8 \\ &= \frac{25-2 a b+16}{2} \\ &= \frac{41-2 a b}{2} \\ &= \frac{41}{2}-a b \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2428
mathedu,mathedu:17d7838d72c7b557,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats an accumulated amount as the principal for subsequent interest calculations,ok,1020 \times[1+(5 \times 0.1)],ok,a sum of money lent out at s . i . amounts to rs . 850 after 2 years and to rs . 1020 after a further period of 5 years . the sum is ?,Assume the interest rate is $x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 850 \times(1+2 x)=1020 \\ & \Rightarrow 1+2 x=1020 \div 850=1.2 \\ & \Rightarrow 2 x=0.2 \\ & \Rightarrow x=0.1 \\ & 1020 \times[1+(5 \times 0.1)] \\ & =1020 \times 1.5 \\ & =1530  \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2437
