mathedu,mathedu:72b6198075a2e779,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Confuses the number of cycles with the total elapsed time,ok,5000 \div 250=20 \text { minutes },ok,"pipe a and pipe b fill water into a tank of capacity 5000 litres , at a rate of 200 l / min and 50 l / min . pipe c drains at a rate of 25 l / min . pipe a is open for 1 min and closed , then pipe b is open for 2 min and closed . further the pipe c is opened and drained for another 2 min . this process is repeated until the tank is filled . how long will it take to fill the tank ?","In every five minutes, $$ \begin{aligned} & 200 \times 1+50 \times 2-25 \times 2=250 \\ & 5000 \div 250=20 \text { minutes } \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2449
mathedu,mathedu:744a328b0400316c,,Comprehension error,Multiplies one value by the number of months instead of summing all values.,ok,6433 \times 5=32165,ok,"a grocer has a sale of rs . 5921 , rs . 5468 , rs . 5568 , rs . 6088 and rs . 6433 for 5 consecutive months . how much sale must he have in the sixth month so that he gets an average sale of rs . 5900 ?",$$ \begin{aligned} & 6433 \times 5=32165 \\ & 5921+5468+5568+6088=23045 \\ & 32165-23043=9120 \end{aligned} $$ $\Rightarrow 9120$ is the sale of $rs$ in fifth mouth $$ \begin{aligned} & 5900 \times 6=35400 \\ & 35400-32165=3235  \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2453
mathedu,mathedu:2c9e898e1a82048a,,Comprehension error,Treats a percentage deficit as a percentage increase,ok,(1.16 x \cdot 1.05 y)-x y,ok,"in measuring the sides of a rectangle , one side is taken 16 % in excess and other 5 % in deficit . find the error percentage in the area calculated from these measurements .",assume the correct sides of the rectangle are $x$ and $y$. $$ \frac{(1.16 x \cdot 1.05 y)-x y}{x y}=\frac{1.218 x y-x y}{x y}=0.218=21.8 \% \# $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2454
mathedu,mathedu:4a70a408fa69aea7,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Rounds the percentage to an inaccurate whole-percent value,ok,\frac{-7}{80.5}\fallingdotseq-0.08=-8 \%,ok,"a camera lens filter kit containing 5 filters sells for $ 87.50 . if the filters are purchased individually , 2 of them are priced at $ 16.45 each , 2 at $ 14.05 each , 1 at $ 19.50 . the amount saved by purchasing the kit is what percent of the total price of the 5 filters purchased individually ?",\begin{aligned} & 2 \times 16.45+2 \times 14.05+19.5=32.9+28.1+19.5=80.5 \\ & \frac{80.5-87.5}{80.5}=\frac{-7}{80.5} \fallingdotseq-0.08=-8 \% \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2457
