mathedu,mathedu:6a455b82169fc0b6,,Unfinished answer,Treats the revenue-to-cost ratio as the percentage gain,ok,x \fallingdotseq 1.27=127 \%,ok,a person bought 110 glass bowls at a rate of rs . 10 per bowl . he sold 100 of them at rs . 14 and the remaining broke . what is the percentage gain for a ?,assume the percentage gain is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} 10 \times 110 x & =14 \times 100 \\ 1100 x & =1400 \\ x & =1400 \div 1100 \\ x & \fallingdotseq 1.27=127 \% \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2524
