mathedu,mathedu:6b41d0b3ced008e3,,Unfinished answer,,label_conflict,2 x=550 \\ & x=275,ok,"a women purchased 3 towels @ rs . 100 each , 5 towels @ rs . 150 each and two towels at a certain rate which is now slipped off from his memory . but she remembers that the average price of the towels was rs . 160 . find the unknown rate of two towels ?",\begin{aligned} & \frac{3 \times 100+5 \times 150+2x}{10}=160 \\ & 1050+2 x=1600 \\ & 2 x=550 \\ & x=275 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2535
mathedu,mathedu:2ebdad2e4db7ab0f,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Incorrectly treats divisors of selected multiples as possible values of n,ok,"divisor of $32 \Rightarrow 1,2,4,8,16,32$ divisor of $64 \Rightarrow 1,2,4,8,16,32,64$",ok,"if an integer n is to be selected at random from 1 to 100 , inclusive , what is probability n ( n + 1 ) will be divisible by 32 ?","divisor of $32 \Rightarrow 1,2,4,8,16,32$ divisor of $64 \Rightarrow 1,2,4,8,16,32,64$ divisor of $96 \Rightarrow 1,2,3,4,6,8,12,16,24,32,48,96$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 32=8 \times 4 \\ & 64=8 \times 8 \\ & 96=8 \times 12 \end{aligned} $$ $n$ dosen't exist.",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2540
