mathedu,mathedu:4f4ca9a3fc11c72a,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Averages mutually exclusive case probabilities instead of adding them,ok,\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{3}{56}+\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{2}{56}+\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{3}{35},ok,"alice , benjamin , and carol each try independently to win a carnival game . if their individual probabilities for success are 1 / 5 , 3 / 8 , and 2 / 7 , respectively , what is the probability that exactly two of the 3 players will win but one will lose ?",\begin{aligned} & \frac{1}{5} \times \frac{3}{8} \times\left(1-\frac{2}{7}\right) \\ & =\frac{1}{5} \times \frac{3}{8} \times \frac{5}{7}=\frac{3}{56} \\ & \frac{1}{5} \times\left(1-\frac{3}{8}\right) \times \frac{2}{7} \\ & =\frac{2}{56} \\ & \left(1-\frac{1}{5}\right) \times \frac{3}{8} \times \frac{2}{7} \\ & =\frac{4}{5} \times \frac{3}{8} \times \frac{2}{7} \\ & =\frac{3}{35} \end{aligned} \begin{aligned} & \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{3}{56}+\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{2}{56}+\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{3}{35} \\ & =\frac{1}{58}+\frac{2}{168}+\frac{3}{105} \\ & =\frac{15+10+24}{840} \\ & =\frac{49}{840} \\ & =\frac{7}{120} \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2550
mathedu,mathedu:b29345c3644d60fe,,Comprehension error,Treats percentage rates as whole-number values instead of decimals,ok,x \times(1+(i+2) \times 5)=-250,ok,"a sum was put a simple interest at a certain rate for 5 years . had it been put at 2 % higher rate , it would have fetched rs . 250 more . the sum is :",assume the sum $X$ $$ \begin{aligned} & x \times(1+i \times 5)-x \times(1+(i+2) \times 5)=-250 \\ & x+5 i x-x-5 i x-10 x=-250 \\ & x=25(rs) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2552
mathedu,mathedu:91640d3ef32afbb1,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses an unweighted average of segment speeds for the overall average speed,ok,\frac{60+\frac{1}{2} \times x}{2}=36,ok,"tom drives from town w to town b , driving at a constant speed of 60 miles per hour . from town b tom immediately continues to town c . the distance between w and b is twice the distance between b and c . if the average speed of the whole journey was 36 mph , then what is tom ' s speed driving from b to c in miles per hour ?",assumes the speed from $b$ to $C X \text {mph }$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{60+\frac{1}{2} \times x}{2}=36 \\ & \frac{1}{2} x=12 \\ & x=24(\mathrm{mph}) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2559
mathedu,mathedu:cec8658d2d072462,,Lack of necessary mathematical concepts,Calculates and sums monthly amounts instead of calculating total interest,ok,100 \times\left(1+\frac{3 \%}{12}\right)+100 \times \left(1+\frac{9 \%}{12}\right),ok,"a sum of rs . 100 is lent at simple interest of 3 % p . a . for the first month , 9 % p . a . for the second month , 27 % p . a . for the third month and so on . what is the total amount of interest earned at the end of the year approximately","\begin{aligned} & \left.100 \times\left(1+\frac{3 \%}{12}\right)+100 \times \left(1+\frac{9 \%}{12}\right) \\ & +\cdots 100 \times\left(1+\frac{(3 \%)^{12}}{12}\right) \\ & a_1=100 \times\left(1+\frac{3 \%}{12}\right), n=12, \\ & a_{12}=100 \times\left(1+\frac{(3 \%)^{12}}{12}\right) \\ & r=3 \end{aligned}",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2563
