mathedu,mathedu:2522359560c1d424,,Comprehension error,Misinterprets “16 more” as 17 more,ok,\frac{12 \times x+16 \times 17}{(x+17)}=15,ok,"at a restaurant , glasses are stored in two different - sized boxes . one box contains 12 glasses , and the other contains 16 glasses . if the average number of glasses per box is 15 , and there are 16 more of the larger boxes , what is the total number of glasses t at the restaurant ? ( assume that all boxes are filled to capacity . )",assume there are $x$ smaller boxes $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{12 \times x+16 \times 17}{(x+17)}=15 \\ & 12 x+272=15 x+255 \\ & 3 x=17 \\ & x=\frac{17}{3} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2636
mathedu,mathedu:c2179e1c5e560387,,Arithmetical error,Makes an arithmetic error when calculating the initial average speed,ok,\frac{80}{2}=45 \text { miles } / \mathrm{hr} .,ok,"car q and car y traveled the same 80 - mile route . if car q took 2 hours and car y traveled at an average speed that was 50 percent faster than the average speed of car q , how many hours did it take car y to travel the route ?",\begin{aligned} & \frac{80}{2}=45 \text { miles } / \mathrm{hr} . \\ & 45 \times(1+50 \%) \\ & =45 \times 1.5 \\ & =67.5 \text { miles } / \mathrm{hr} \\ & 80 \div 67.5=\frac{80}{67.5}=\frac{16}{13.5} = 1.19 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2640
mathedu,mathedu:f1ffdd85d8280092,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Subtracts pairwise overlap counts without properly accounting for triple overlap,ok,46-7-4-5=30,ok,"in a class of 50 students , 20 play baseball , 15 play cricket and 11 play football . 7 play both baseball and cricket , 4 play cricket and football and 5 play baseball and football . if 18 students do not play any of these given sports , how many students play exactly two of these sports ?",$$ \begin{aligned} & 20+15+11=46 \\ & 46-7-4-5=30 \\ & 50-18=32 \\ & 32-30=2 \\ & 2 \div 2=1 \end{aligned} $$ So there are $7+4+5-1 \times 2=13$ students play two sports,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2643
