mathedu,mathedu:9e68ee135c948dcc,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats excess coverage as area without accounting for extra layers,ok,280-180=100 \Rightarrow$ excessive paper $$ 100-36=64,ok,"three walls have wallpaper covering a combined area of 280 square meters . by overlapping the wallpaper to cover a wall with an area of 180 square meters , the area that is covered by exactly two layers of wallpaper is 36 square meters . what is the area that is covered with three layers of wallpaper ?",280 \Rightarrow$ the whole area of wall paper $280-180=100 \Rightarrow$ excessive paper $$ 100-36=64 \Rightarrow \text { remaining paper } $$ $$ \text { Ans: } 64 \mathrm{~m}^2 $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2684
