mathedu,mathedu:e68030f738de0436,,Arithmetical error,Makes an arithmetic error when solving the final linear equation,ok,110 a=550 \ & a=50 .,ok,machine a and machine b are each used to manufacture 550 sprockets . it takes machine a 10 hours longer to produce 550 sprockets than machine b . machine b produces 10 percent more sprockets per hour than machine a . how many sprockets per hour does machine a produces ?,"machine a manufacture a sprockets per hour , machine $b$ manufacture $b$ sprockets per hour $t$ hours for machine $b$ to manufacture 550 sprocket. $$ \begin{aligned} & b=1.1 a \\ & a(t+10)=b t \\ & a t+10 a=1.1 a t=550 \\ & 10 a=0.1 a t \\ & 100 a=a t \\ & 110 a=550 \\ & a=50 . \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2694
