mathedu,mathedu:273cdd2306c65e66,,Comprehension error,Ignores one rate's contribution during the interval when both operate,ok,\frac{\left(1-\frac{1}{10} \times 2\right)}{\frac{1}{15}},ok,"two pipes p and q can fill a cistern in 10 and 15 minutes respectively . both are opened together , but at the end of 2 minutes the first is turned off . how many more minutes will it take for the cistern to fill after the first pipe is turned off ?","speed of $p:\frac{1}{10}$, speed of $q: \frac{1}{15}$ $$ \frac{\left(1-\frac{1}{10} \times 2\right)}{\frac{1}{15}}=\frac{\frac{4}{5}}{\frac{1}{15}}=12(\mathrm{~min}) $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2700
mathedu,mathedu:560b6d8bcc938b06,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Applies percentage changes directly to a reciprocal rate instead of unit price.,ok,\frac{x-48}{48}=4 \%,ok,if a man lost 4 % by selling oranges at the rate of 48 a rupee at how many a rupee must he sell them to gain 44 % ?,assume the cost $x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{x-48}{48}=4 \% \\ & x=67.2 \end{aligned} $$ selling at y $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{y-67-2}{y}=44 \% \\ & 0.56 y=67.2 \\ & y=120(rs) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2704
mathedu,mathedu:0462b2c07bea6cdf,,Unfinished answer,Stops after deriving an intermediate relationship without calculating the requested time,ok,\therefore & 4 x=8 y,ok,"an electric pump can fill a tank in 4 hours . because of a leak in the tank , it took 8 hours to fill the tank . if the tank is full , how much time will the leak take to empty it ?",Assume the electric pump fill $x$ liter per hour \& the tank empty $y$ liter per hour $$ \begin{aligned} & 4 x=8(x-y) \\ \Rightarrow & 4 x=8 x-8 y \\ \Rightarrow & 4 x=8 y \\ \Rightarrow & x=2 y \\ \because & x=2 y \\ \therefore & 4 x=8 y \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2707
