mathedu,mathedu:8c916aaab0d6bd14,,Unfinished answer,Computes total completion time instead of the requested completed fraction,ok,\frac{90 r}{3 r+2 r}=\frac{90 r}{5 r}=18 \text { (days) },ok,"two persons a and b can complete a piece of work in 30 days and 45 days respectively . if they work together , what part of the work will be completed in 3 days ?","$$ \because[30,45]=90 $$ $\therefore$ assume the total workload is 90r. daily workload $\left\{\begin{array}{l}a: 3 r \\ b: 2 r\end{array}\right.$ $$ \frac{90 r}{3 r+2 r}=\frac{90 r}{5 r}=18 \text { (days) } $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2743
