mathedu,mathedu:70cba7ff1a7284ca,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses selling price instead of cost price as the gain-percentage denominator,ok,\frac{y-800}{y}=10 \%,ok,"boy sells a book for rs . 720 he gets a loss of 10 % , to gain 10 % , what should be the sp ?","assume the original sp $X$, new $s p=y$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{720-x}{x}=10 \% \\ & 0.9 x=720 \\ & x=800 \\ & \frac{y-800}{y}=10 \% \\ & 0.9 y=800 \\ & y = 800 \times \frac{10}{9} = 723 \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2788
