mathedu,mathedu:388194d34590fb13,,Comprehension error,Computes the least common multiple using rounds instead of lap times,ok,the least common multiple between $40 \& 90$ is 360,ok,"the racing magic takes 150 seconds to circle the racing track once . the charging bull makes 40 rounds of the track in an hour . if they left the starting point together , how many minutes will it take for them to meet at the starting point for the second time ?",40 rounds of the track in an hour. $$ \Rightarrow 60 \times 60 \div 40=\frac{3600}{40}=90 $$ $\Rightarrow$ the charging bull takes 90 seconds to circle the track once. the least common multiple between $40 \& 90$ is 360 360 seconds $=6$ minutes,dataset/time_series_split/train.json#2804
