mathedu,mathedu:c4270fea5b13d849,,Comprehension error,Confuses a decrease in selling price with the selling price itself,ok,\frac{8.40-(1-20 \%) x}{(1-20 \%) x} =30 \%,ok,"a man sells an article at a profit of 25 % . if he had bought it at 20 % less and sold it for rs . 8.40 less , he would have gained 30 % . find the cost of the article .",assume the cost of the article is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} \frac{8.40-(1-20 \%) x}{(1-20 \%) x} & =30 \% \\ 8.40-0.8 x & =0.24 x \\ 8.40 & =1.04 x \\ x & \fallingdotseq 8.08 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/val.json#52
