mathedu,mathedu:623fbb70230bad3e,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses the removed fraction instead of the remaining fraction,ok,0.6 x=0.3 x+\left(1-\frac{y}{100}\right) 0.7 x,ok,"the weight of a glass of jar is 30 % of the weight of the jar filled with coffee beans . after some of the beans have been removed , the weight of the jar and the remaining beans is 60 % of the original total weight . what fraction part of the beans remain in the jar ?","assume jar filled with coffee beans is $x$, and $y \%$ of beans remained after removing some part of beans. jar filled with coffee beans $\left\{\begin{array}{l}\text { jar: } 0.3 x \\ \text { coffee beans : } 0.7 x\end{array}\right.$ $$ 0.6 x=0.3 x+\left(1-\frac{y}{100}\right) 0.7 x $$ $0.3 x=0.7 x-\frac{0.7 x y}{100}$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 300=700-7 y \\ & 7 y=400 \end{aligned} $$ $y=\frac{400}{7} \Rightarrow \frac{400}{7}$ of beans were remain. ",dataset/time_series_split/val.json#78
mathedu,mathedu:6a3bc2e54d4c4c2e,,Algebraic error,Makes an algebraic rearrangement error when solving a linear equation,ok,r=\frac{4}{3} r-2400 \quad & r=2400,ok,a leak in the bottom of a tank can empty the full tank in 6 hours . an inlet pipe fills water at the rate of 5 liters per minute . when the tank is full in inlet is opened and due to the leak the tank is empties in 8 hours . the capacity of the tank is ?,assume the capacity of the tank is $r$ liters. $\left\{\begin{array}{l}\text { water injection per hour: } 5 \times 60=300 \text { (liters) } \\ \text { water discharge per hour: } \frac{r}{6} \text { (liters) }\end{array}\right.$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 8=\frac{r}{\frac{r}{6}-300} \\ & r=\frac{4}{3} r-2400 \\ & r=2400 \text { (liters)  } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/val.json#83
