mathedu,mathedu:512ace580d9c9230,,Comprehension error,Treats interest and discount amounts as total accumulated or present values,ok,x \times\left(1+i \right)=90 \quad \frac{x}{(1+i)}=80,ok,the simple interest and the true discount on a certain sum for a given time and at a given rate are rs . 90 and rs . 80 respectively . the sum is :,"assume the sum x,rate = i \\\begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array}{l} x \times\left(1+i \right)=90 \\ \frac{x}{(1+i)}=80 \end{array}\right. \\ & \left\{\begin{array}{l} x=\frac{90}{1+i} \\ x=80 \times\left(1+i \right) \end{array}\right. \\ & \frac{90}{1+i }=80\left(1+i \right) \end{aligned}\begin{aligned} & \left(1+i \right)^2=\frac{9}{8} \\ & 1+i=\frac{3}{\sqrt{8}} \\ & x=80 \times \frac{3}{\sqrt{8}} \\ & =80 \times \frac{3 \sqrt{2}}{2 \sqrt{2} \times \sqrt{2}} \\ & =60 \sqrt{2} \end{aligned}",dataset/time_series_split/val.json#128
