mathedu,mathedu:4c16fca2d01c6a17,,Lack of necessary mathematical concepts,Treats exponentiation as multiplication by the exponent,ok,3 x \cdot 4 y=531441,ok,"if 3 ^ x * 4 ^ y = 531,441 and x – y = 12 , then x = ?",$$ \begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array}{l} 3 x \cdot 4 y=531441 \ldots (1) \\ x-y=12 \ldots(2) \end{array}\right. \\ & \text { (2) } \Rightarrow y=x-12 \ldots(3) \end{aligned} $$ substitute $(x-12)$ for $y$ in (1) $$ \begin{aligned} \Rightarrow 3 x \cdot 4(x-12) & =531441 \\ x(x-12) & =\frac{531441}{3 \times 4} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/val.json#162
