mathedu,mathedu:634db097bc9eca0c,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Models combined production using completion times instead of reciprocal rates,ok,\left(\frac{5}{4} w \div w\right)[t+(t+2)] =3,ok,"running at their respective constant rate , machine x takes 2 days longer to produce w widgets than machines y . at these rates , if the two machines together produce 5 w / 4 widgets in 3 days , how many days would it take machine x alone to produce 6 w widgets .",assume machine $y$ takes $t$ days to produce $w$ widgets. $$ \begin{aligned} \left(\frac{5}{4} w \div w\right)[t+(t+2)] & =3 \\ \frac{5}{4}(2 t+2) & =3 \\ \frac{10}{4} t & =3-\frac{10}{4} \\ 10 t & =12-10 \\ t & =\frac{1}{5} \end{aligned} $$ machine $x$ produce alone: $\frac{6 w \div w}{\frac{1}{5}+2}=6 \times \frac{5}{11}=\frac{30}{11} \fallingdotseq 2.73$ (days),dataset/time_series_split/val.json#218
