mathedu,mathedu:b5cafe3b28bba495,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Divides annual interest rates by the number of years,ok,5000 \times\left(\frac{5 \%}{2}-\frac{4 \%}{2}\right),ok,a person borrows rs . 5000 for 2 years at 4 % p . a . simple interest . he immediately lends it to another person at 5 % p . a for 2 years . find his gain in the transaction per year .,\begin{aligned} & 5000 \times\left(\frac{5 \%}{2}-\frac{4 \%}{2}\right) \\ & =5000 \times 0.5 \% \\ & =25 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/val.json#244
mathedu,mathedu:59163c137d70538a,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats a quantity that is 120% bigger as merely 120% of the original,ok,the capacity of truck's tank $=65 \times 120 \%=78$,ok,"in a fuel station the service costs $ 2.20 per vehicle and every liter of fuel costs $ 0.70 . assuming that you fill up 3 mini - vans and 2 trucks , what will be the total cost , if a mini - van ' s tank is 65 liters and a truck ' s tank is 120 % bigger and they are all empty ?",the capacity of truck's tank $=65 \times 120 \%=78$ $$ \begin{aligned} \text { the total cost } & =2.20(3+2)+0.7[(3 \times 65)+(2 \times 78)] \\ & =11+245.7 \\ & =256.7(\$) \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/val.json#256
mathedu,mathedu:84d96079d656f6ee,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Multiplies complementary events as if they were independent,ok,=\left(1-\frac{7}{100}\right)\left(1-\frac{8}{100}\right),ok,"a certain bag contains 100 balls â € ” 50 white , 25 green , 10 yellow , 7 red , and 8 purple . if a ball is to be chosen at random , what is the probability that the ball will be neither red nor purple ?",811 the probability of drawing a $\left\{\begin{array}{l}\text { red ball : } \frac{7}{100} \\ \text { purple ball : } \frac{8}{100}\end{array}\right.$ $\therefore$ the probability that the ball will be neither red nor purple $$ \begin{aligned} & =\left(1-\frac{7}{100}\right)\left(1-\frac{8}{100}\right) \\ & =\frac{93 \times 92}{10000} \\ & =\frac{8556}{10000}  \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/val.json#259
