mathedu,mathedu:ff817275fc83d35c,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Adds completion times instead of combining reciprocal work rates,ok,\frac{100}{20}(x+x+2) =\frac{100}{25} \times 3,ok,"machine c takes 2 more hours than machine b to make 20 widgets . if working together , the machines can make 25 widgets in 3 hours , how long will it take machine c to make 40 widgets ?","$$ \begin{aligned} & 20+20=40 \\ & {[40,25]=100} \end{aligned} $$ assume machine $c$ takes $X$ hours to make 20 widgets. $$ \begin{aligned} \frac{100}{20}(x+x+2) & =\frac{100}{25} \times 3 \\ 5 x & =12-10 \\ x & =0.4 \end{aligned} $$ $$ \frac{40}{20} \times 0.4=0.8(\mathrm{hrs}) \# $$",dataset/time_series_split/val.json#279
