mathedu,mathedu:1b40c931626d0859,,Unfinished answer,Reports the required total workforce instead of the additional workforce,ok,x=125 \text { (workers) },ok,"an engineer undertakes a project to build a road 15 km long in 300 days and employs 50 men for the purpose . after 100 days , he finds only 2.5 km of the road has been completed . find the ( approximate ) number of extra men he must employ to finish the work in time .",$\frac{2.5 \mathrm{~km}}{50 \times 100}=\frac{2.5}{5000}$ per work per day $300-100=200$ days left $$ \begin{aligned} & x \times 200 \times \frac{2.5}{5000}=15-2.5 \\ & 0.1 x=12.5 \\ & x=125 \text { (workers) } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/val.json#300
mathedu,mathedu:9f1b43cf2c17b858,,Arithmetical error,"Rounds a repeating quotient prematurely, producing an inaccurate final value.",ok,x^2-6.25=\frac{44}{6} \quad ... \quad =13.58,ok,the perimeter of a triangle is 44 cm and the inradius of the triangle is 2.5 cm . what is the area of the triangle ?,\begin{aligned} & \left(x^2-2.5^2\right) \times 6=44 \\ & x^2-6.25=\frac{44}{6} \\ & x^2 = 6.25+7.33 \\ & =13.58 \end{aligned} \begin{aligned} & x^2-2.5^2 \\ & =13.58-6.25 \\ & =7.33 \\ & \frac{7.33 \times 2.5 \times 6}{2}  \\ & =7.33 \times 7.5 \\ & =54.975 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/val.json#305
