mathedu,mathedu:808a3d021924aff5,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Calculates profit percentages using selling price instead of cost price,ok,92 \times 15 \% =13.8,ok,"a certain manufacturer increased its gross profit on a product from 10 percent of the cost of the product to 15 percent of the cost by changing the selling price . if the new selling price was $ 92.00 and the cost of the product remained the same , what was the old selling price ?",\begin{aligned} & 92 \times 15 \% \\ & =13.8 \\ & 92-13.8=78.2 \Rightarrow \text { the costs } \\ & \text { original price }=x \\ & \frac{x-78.2}{x}=10 \% \\ & 0.9 x=78.2 \\ & x=78.2 \times \frac{10}{9} \\ & \= 86.89 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/val.json#312
