mathedu,mathedu:8ef236c2ef6f065e,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Treats compound growth as linear multiplication by time rather than repeated compounding,ok,compound interest : x(1+10 %) \cdot 2=2.2 x,ok,if difference between compound interest and simple interest on a sum at 10 % p . a . for 2 years is rs . 150 then sum is,assume the investment amount is $x$ initially. $$ \begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array}{l} \text { compound interest : } x(1+10 \%) \cdot 2=2.2 x \\ \text { simple interest : } x+2 x \cdot 10 \%=1.2 x \end{array}\right. \\ & \begin{aligned} 2.2 x-1.2 x=150 \\ x=150 \end{aligned} \end{aligned} $$ the sum $=(1.2+2.2) \times 150=3.4 \times 150=510$,dataset/time_series_split/val.json#340
