mathedu,mathedu:430a67cbace933d0,,Unfinished answer,"Reports only the remaining joint-work time, omitting the initial solo-work period",ok,=6 \text { (days)  },ok,p and q can complete a work in 20 days and 12 days respectively . p alone started the work and q joined him after 4 days till the completion of the work . how long did the work last ?,"$$ (20,12)=60 $$ assume the total workload is 60r. $$ \begin{aligned} & \text { daily workload }\left\{\begin{array}{l} p: \frac{60 r}{20}=3 r \\ q: \frac{60 r}{12}=5 r \end{array}\right. \\ & \frac{60 r-4 \times 3 r}{3 r+5 r}=\frac{48 r}{8 r}=6 \text { (days)  } \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/test.json#47
