mathedu,mathedu:91ceeb1db2d98488,,Arithmetical error,Miscomputes the quotient when dividing the scaled distance.,ok,\frac{8800}{9} & = 988.8 \cdots,ok,a can give b 100 meters start and c 120 meters start in a kilometer race . how much start can b give c in a kilometer race ?,Assume the length of the race is $1000 \mathrm{~m}$ $A$ runs $1000 \mathrm{~m}$ when $b$ runs $900 \mathrm{~m} \& c$ runs $880 \mathrm{~m}$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \begin{aligned} \frac{880 \times 1000}{900}=\frac{880 \times 10}{9}=\frac{8800}{9} & =988.8 \cdots \\ & = 988.89 \mathrm{~m} \end{aligned} \\ & 1000-988.89=11.11 \mathrm{~m} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#70
