mathedu,mathedu:797162bb4514a625,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Uses the original completion time instead of the modified schedule,ok,24(x+y)-18(x+y)=6(x+y),ok,a man and a boy complete a work together in 24 days . if for the last 6 days man alone does the work then it is completed in 26 days . how long the boy will take to complete the work alone ?,"Assume the man can do $X$ perday, boy can do $y$ per day. $24(x+y) \Rightarrow$ total work load. $$ \begin{aligned} & 24(x+y)-18(x+y)=6(x+y) \Rightarrow \text { remaining work, } \\ & 6(x+y) \div x=26 \\ & \Rightarrow(x+y) \div x=\frac{13}{3} \\ & \Rightarrow 1+\frac{y}{x}=\frac{13}{3} \\ & \Rightarrow \frac{y}{x}=\frac{10}{3} \\ & \Rightarrow 10 x=3 y \Rightarrow x=\frac{3 y}{10} \\ & 24(x+y) \div y \\ & =24\left(\frac{3 y}{10}+y\right) \div y \\ & =24 \cdot \frac{13}{10}=31.2 \text { days } \end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/test.json#202
mathedu,mathedu:438e356f875ba034,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Adds the intersection when computing a union instead of subtracting it,ok,x+\frac{1}{2} x+x \cdot \frac{1}{2} x =12\left(x \cdot \frac{1}{2} x\right),ok,"the events a and b are independent , the probability that event a occurs is greater than 0 , and the probability that event a occurs is twice the probability that event b occurs . the probability that at least one of events a and b occurs is 12 times the probability that both events a and b occur . what is the probability that event a occurs ?",assume the probability that event a occurs is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} x+\frac{1}{2} x+x \cdot \frac{1}{2} x & =12\left(x \cdot \frac{1}{2} x\right) \\ \frac{11}{2} x^2-\frac{3}{2} x & =0 \\ \frac{11}{2} x\left(x-\frac{3}{11}\right) & =0 \\ x & =\frac{3}{11} \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#204
