mathedu,mathedu:cd7902111c4c1841,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,,label_conflict,320-20 \times(12-1)=100,ok,"a prize of $ 800 is to be distributed among 20 winners , each of whom must be awarded at least $ 20 . if 2 / 5 of the prize will be distributed to 3 / 5 of the winners , what is the greatest possible individual award ?",\begin{aligned} & 800 \times \frac{2}{5}=320 \\ & 20 \times \frac{3}{5}=12 \\ & 320-20 \times(12-1)=100 \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/test.json#289
mathedu,mathedu:b80056fca0253f7b,,Algebraic error,Fails to distribute multiplication across both terms in parentheses,ok,39-x =2 x-9,ok,the sum of the present age of henry and jill is 48 . what is their present ages if 9 years ago henry was twice the age of jill ?,assume jill is $x$ years old now. $$ \begin{aligned} (48-x) & -9=2(x-9) \\ 39-x & =2 x-9 \\ 3 x & =48 \\ x & =16 \text { (years old )  } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#292
mathedu,mathedu:03734af9420adc13,,Comprehension error,Treats a percentage of valid votes as a percentage of total votes,ok,=6000(1-55 \%-20 \%),ok,"in an election between two candidates , one got 55 % of the total valid votes , 20 % of the votes were invalid . if the total number of votes was 6000 , the number of valid votes that the other candidate got , was :",valid votes that the other candidate got $$ \begin{aligned} & =6000(1-55 \%-20 \%) \\ & =6000 \times 0.25 \\ & =1500  \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#295
mathedu,mathedu:2ab28425bdfdf522,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Misinterprets a two-period total as twice one period’s expenditure,ok,(1-x \%)=2 \cdot(1.2-2 x \%),ok,"a man saves a certain portion of his income during a year and spends the remaining portion on his personal expenses . next year his income increases by 20 % but his savings increase by 100 % . if his total expenditure in 2 years is double his expenditure in 1 st year , what % age of his income in the first year did he save ?",Assume the man's income is 1 \& he save $x \%$ of his income. $$ \begin{aligned} & (1-x \%)=2 \cdot(1.2-2 x \%) \\ & \Rightarrow 1-x \%=2.4-4 x \% \\ & \Rightarrow 3 x \%=1.4 \\ & \Rightarrow x \%=\frac{14}{30}=\frac{7}{15} = 0.47=47 \%  \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#305
mathedu,mathedu:c9ebd8e5f3cfd724,,Unfinished answer,Confuses the retained price factor with the discount percentage,ok,y & =0.9=90 \%,ok,a merchant marks goods up by 75 % and then offers a discount on the marked price . the profit that the merchant makes after offering the discount is 57.5 % . what % discount did the merchant offer ?,"assume the cost of the goods is $r$, and merchant offered $\chi \%$ discount. $$ \begin{aligned} \frac{[(1+75 \%) r] y-r}{r \quad} & =57.5 \% \\ 1.75 r y-r & =0.575 r \\ 1.75 y-1 & =0.575 \\ 1.75 y & =1.575 \\ y & =0.9=90 \%\end{aligned} $$",dataset/time_series_split/test.json#306
