mathedu,mathedu:0233b36a7105b142,,Comprehension error,Applies a percentage increase to the original price instead of the purchase price,ok,selling price }=1.5 x,ok,a trader bought a car at 30 % discount on its original price . he sold it at a 50 % increase on the price he bought it . what percent of profit did he make on the original price ?,assume the original price X $$ \begin{aligned} & \text { costs: } 0.7 x \\ & \text { selling price }=1.5 x \\ & \frac{1.5 x-0.7 x}{x} \\ & =80 \% \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#316
