mathedu,mathedu:6e8c761f9ca95268,,Careless error,Miscounts group size when applying averages after members join or leave,ok,42-[31m\frac{31 \times 11-30 \times 9}{2}=6.5,ok,"when a student joe , weighing 42 kg , joins a group of students whose average weight is 30 kg , the average weight goes up by 1 kg . subsequently , if two students , excluding joe , leave the group the average weight comes back to 30 kg . what is the difference between the average weight of the two students who left and the weight of joe ?",Students is $x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{42+30 x}{x+1}=31 \\ & 42+30 x=31 x+31 \\ & x=11 \\ & 42-\frac{31 \times 11-30 \times 9}{2}=6.5 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#368
mathedu,mathedu:231c0f33dd6d1360,,Algebraic error,Subtracts incorrectly when solving for the unknown length,ok,135+x=375 \ & x=340,ok,"the length of the bridge , which a train 135 m long and traveling at 45 km / hr can cross in 30 sec is ?",Assume the length of bridge is $x \mathrm{~m}$ $$ \begin{aligned} & 45 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr}=45 \times 1000 \div 60 \div 60=12.5 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s} \\ & (135+x) \div 12.5=30 \\ & 135+x=375 \\ & x=340 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#370
