mathedu,mathedu:810a80796388b01b,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Calculates profit percentage using revenue instead of cost.,ok,profit $=\frac{48 x+1920-50 x-1400}{48 x+1920}=20 \%$,ok,how many pounds of salt at 50 cents / lb must be mixed with 40 lbs of salt that costs 35 cents / lb so that a merchant will get 20 % profit by selling the mixture at 48 cents / lb ?,assume there are $X$ ponds 50 cents/lb salt $$ \begin{aligned} & \begin{aligned} \costs & =50 \times x+40 \times 35 \\ & =50 x+1400 \end{aligned} \\ & \begin{aligned} \text { revenue } & =48 \times(x+40) \\ & =48 x+1920 \end{aligned} \\ & \text { profit }=\frac{48 x+1920-50 x-1400}{48 x+1920}=20 \% \\ & -2 x+520=9.6 x+384 \\ &   11.6 x=136 \\ &  x = 11.72 \text { (pounds) } \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#432
