mathedu,mathedu:a67f09d522d44c49,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Combines pairwise ratio changes by altering individual terms incorrectly,ok,new ratio of the solution =6: 12.5: 100=12: 25: 200,ok,"the ratio , by volume , of bleach to detergent to water in a certain solution is 2 : 25 : 100 . the solution will be altered so that the ratio of bleach to detergent is tripled while the ratio of detergent to water is halved . if the altered solution will contain 300 liters of water , how many liters of detergent will it contain ?",\begin{aligned} & \text { new ratio of the solution }=6: 12.5: 100=12: 25: 200 \\ & \begin{aligned} \text { detergent } \Rightarrow & 300 \times \frac{25}{12+25+200} \\ & =300 \times \frac{25}{237} \\ & = 31.65(\text { liters }) \end{aligned} \end{aligned},dataset/time_series_split/test.json#465
mathedu,mathedu:28e6084c43fbe4c1,,Algebraic error,Divides incorrectly when solving the linear equation,ok,5 x =720 \quad \ x =124,ok,a sports retailer ordered white and yellow tennis balls in equal number but the dispatch clerk of the tennis ball company erred and dispatched 90 extra yellow balls and making ratio of white balls to yellow balls 8 / 13 . how many tennis balls did the retailer order originally .,assam the retailer ordered x yellow and white tennis ball respectively. $$ \begin{aligned} x: x+90 & =8: 13 \\ 8 x+720 & =13 x \\ 5 x & =720 \\ x & =124 \end{aligned} $$ $\Rightarrow$ the total number of tennis ball that the retailer ordered: $2 \times 124=248$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#467
