mathedu,mathedu:dfd7e1ba59d85b0b,,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,Applies successive percentage increases inconsistently instead of combining them correctly,ok,x \cdot(1+25 \%)=30 ... 24 \cdot(1+20 \%) = 28.8,ok,"the marked price of a book is 20 % more than the cost price . after the book is sold , the vendor realizes that he had wrongly raised the cost price by a margin of 25 % . if the marked price of the book is rs . 30 , what is the original cost price of the book ?",Assume the cost is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} & x \cdot(1+25 \%)=30 \\ \Rightarrow & 1.25 x=30 \\ \Rightarrow & x=24 \\ & 24 \cdot(1+20 \%) \\ = & 24 \times 1.2 \\ = & 28.8 \end{aligned} $$,dataset/time_series_split/test.json#515
