 5500",dataset/dataset.json#5 dataset/dataset.json#787
stepwise,stepwise:bd172080107a4caa,,Extra quantity or Missing quantity,Omits a preceding multiplication when applying successive growth factors,ok,"In the second year, the colony tripled, so it became 3*X.",ok,"A group of researchers are studying a colony of penguins. Their results show that the size doubled in the first year they watched the colony, then tripled in the next year. This year, however, harsh conditions meant the colony only gained 129 penguins. The colony has 1077 penguins in it now. Each penguin eats one and a half fish every day. How many fish did the whole colony catch per day to eat at the beginning of the first year?","Let X be the number of penguins in the beginning of the first year.
In the second year, the colony tripled, so it became 3*X.
In the third year, the colony gained 129 penguins, so it became 3*X + 129.
We know that 3*X + 129 = 1077, so 3*X = 948, and X = 316.
So at the beginning of the first year, the colony had 316 penguins.
Therefore, the colony caught 316 * 1.5 = 474 fish per day to eat.
 474",dataset/dataset.json#6
stepwise,stepwise:5a4196ddda4786b0,,Misunderstanding of a question,Assumes each sandwich requires multiple croissants instead of one croissant.,ok,"Thus, she needs 48 x 2 = 96 mini croissants.",ok,"For the gala luncheon planning committee, Margaret wants to serve chicken salad sandwiches using mini croissants.  She wants there to be enough food that each person on the committee can have 2 sandwiches each.  Her bakery offers 12 minis croissants for $8.00.  There are 24 people on the committee. How much will she spend on croissants?","Margaret needs to make 2 x 24 = 48 mini croissant sandwiches.
The bakery offers 12 mini croissants for $8.00, so each sandwich needs 2 croissants.
Thus, she needs 48 x 2 = 96 mini croissants.
She will need to buy 96/12 = 8 sets of 12 mini croissants.
So, she will spend 8 x $8.00 = $64.00 on croissants.
 64.00",dataset/dataset.json#7
stepwise,stepwise:8f94d191aaff2660,,Missing / Wrong factual knowledge,Assigns the known amount to the wrong ratio component,ok,we can substitute y = 50: 2:1:3 = x:50:50,ok,"Sam shared a sum of money between his three cousins Sandra, Amy and Ruth in the ratio 2:1:3 respectively. If Amy got $50, how much did Sandra get?","We can start by setting up a proportion:
2:1:3 = x:50:y
