 56.67",dataset/dataset.json#69
stepwise,stepwise:c2bd75cb16b5058d,,Misunderstanding of a question,Scales quantity by budget change without accounting for changed unit cost,ok,they can buy (1.2 x 15) = 18 softballs,ok,"The school decided to add 20% to the gym budget. In a normal month, they could buy 15 dodgeballs for $5 each if they spent the entire budget on that. If they only buy softballs instead, which cost $9 each, how many can they buy with the new budget?","If the school adds 20% to the gym budget, the new budget will be 100% + 20% = 120% of the original budget.
