stepwise,stepwise:2e73ff4e07bd6a0f,,Misunderstanding of a question,Uses the remaining amount instead of the total amount for a full-capacity calculation,ok,"Therefore, with 8 gallons of gas left in the tank, she can drive 25 x 8 = 200 miles on a single tank of gas.",ok,"Sophia is thinking of taking a road trip in her car, and would like to know how far she can drive on a single tank of gas. She has traveled 100 miles since last filling her tank, and she needed to put in 4 gallons of gas to fill it up again. The owner's manual for her car says that her tank holds 12 gallons of gas. How many miles can Sophia drive on a single tank of gas?","Sophia used 4 out of the 12 gallons of gas in her tank, so there are 12-4 = 8 gallons of gas left in the tank.
