stepwise,stepwise:c26fd7cb8e8fe393,,Misunderstanding of a question,Confuses a fraction of each interval with minutes when summing intervals,ok,"Therefore, Jason shoots flames for 4 x 1/3 = 4/3 minutes per minute.",ok,"When Jason plays the video game, Duty for Ashes, his mission to slay the dragon hoard requires that he fire his weapon on average every 15 seconds.   And each time he fires his weapon, his power-fire setting allows him to shoot a flame for 5 seconds.  On average, how many seconds per minute does Jason shoot flames at the dragon hoard?","Jason fires his weapon every 15 seconds, so he shoots flames for 5 seconds every 15 seconds. This means he shoots flames for 5/15 = 1/3 of each 15-second interval.
