 5",dataset/dataset.json#708 dataset/dataset.json#966
stepwise,stepwise:e180d0717a9ca41f,,Reached correct solution but proceeded further,Subtracts the amount taken from the original total instead of reporting it,ok,"Therefore, the squirrel has 210 - 30 = 180 acorns to eat",ok,"A squirrel had stashed 210 acorns to last him the three winter months. It divided the pile into thirds, one for each month, and then took some from each third, leaving 60 acorns for each winter month. The squirrel combined the ones it took to eat in the first cold month of spring before plants were in bloom again. How many acorns does the squirrel have to eat at the beginning of spring?","The squirrel had 210/3 = 70 acorns for each winter month initially.
