 300",dataset/dataset.json#711
stepwise,stepwise:6f75208c1f3ef065,,Extra quantity or Missing quantity,Omits an initial purchase cost when calculating total out-of-pocket expense,ok,Jim is out of pocket for the wife's ring minus the money he made from selling his ring,ok,"Jim buys a wedding ring for $10,000.  He gets his wife a ring that is twice that much and sells the first one for half its value.  How much is he out of pocket?","The wife's ring is twice the price of Jim's ring, so it costs 2 x $10,000 = $20,000.
