In three years, Talia's father will be the same age as Talia's mom is today, so he will be 39 + 3 = 42 years old.
Currently, Talia's father is 42 - 3 = 39 years old.
 39",dataset/dataset.json#790
stepwise,stepwise:5e7a72abc3cf1ce3,,Missing / Wrong factual knowledge,Fails to apply both travel segments to every day,ok,"Using the same speed for Wednesday-Saturday, the driver travels 25 x 4 = 100 miles per day.",ok,A driver travels 30 miles per hour for 3 hours and 25 miles per hour for 4 hours to deliver goods to a town every day from Monday to Saturday. How many miles does the driver travel in a week?,"On Monday, the driver travels 30 x 3 = 90 miles.
On Tuesday, the driver travels 25 x 4 = 100 miles.
Using the same speed for Wednesday-Saturday, the driver travels 25 x 4 = 100 miles per day.
From Wednesday to Saturday, the driver travels 100 x 4 = 400 miles.
In a week, the driver travels 90 + 100 + 400 = 590 miles.
 590",dataset/dataset.json#794
stepwise,stepwise:9894022bca37b21b,,Missing / Wrong factual knowledge,Reverses the stated twice-as-many relationship between two quantities,ok,"If the number of adult men was twice the number of adult women, then the number of adult women was 600/2 = 300",ok,"The community leader of a certain town organized a cleaning day event where community members were to be involved in collecting trash inside the town. Out of 2000 community members involved in the cleaning process, 30% were adult men. If there were twice as many adult women as adult men in the event, and the rest were children, calculate the total number of children involved in the cleaning event.","Out of the 2000 community members, 30/100*2000 = 600 were adult men.
If the number of adult men was twice the number of adult women, then the number of adult women was 600/2 = 300
The total number of adult men and women involved in the event is 600+300 = 900
The rest of the community members involved in the cleaning event were children, which is 2000-900 = 1100 children. 
 1100",dataset/dataset.json#795
stepwise,stepwise:4934a305c8ac0e60,,Extra quantity or Missing quantity,"Adds the original total to the updated total, double-counting the original quantity",ok,"Therefore, it will take Hansel 75 + 105 = 180 minutes",ok,"Hansel has a created album on Spotify that contains 25 songs and each song is 3 minutes long. If she adds 10 more songs to the album with the same duration, how many minutes will it take her to finish all the songs in the album?","The total duration of the original 25 songs is 25 x 3 = 75 minutes.
The total duration of the album after adding 10 more songs is (25 + 10) x 3 = 105 minutes.
Therefore, it will take Hansel 75 + 105 = 180 minutes to finish all the songs in the album.
 180",dataset/dataset.json#796
stepwise,stepwise:cd5aa67d4972da8a,,Missing / Wrong factual knowledge,Uses the number of kits to calculate students instead of the given class size,ok,there are 20 x 2 = 40 students in total,ok,"Liam is teaching art to a group of 10 students. He has 20 art kits that he hands out to the students to share, 1 art kit for 2 students. From those art kits half the students make 3 artworks each and half the students make 4 artworks each. How many artistic works does the whole class create?","Each art kit is shared by 2 students, so there are 20 x 2 = 40 students in total.
