 48",dataset/dataset.json#803 dataset/dataset.json#948
stepwise,stepwise:de41478bdbb50620,,Missing / Wrong factual knowledge,Double-counts the number of airplanes when calculating daily capacity,ok,"Therefore, the airline company can accommodate a total of 700 x 10 = 7000 passengers each day.",ok,An airline company owns 5 airplanes. Every airplane they own has 20 rows with 7 seats in each row. Each airplane makes 2 flights a day. How many passengers can the airline company accommodate each day?,"Each airplane has a total of 20 x 7 = 140 seats.
