In ten years, Rena will be 5 years older than Pam, so R + 10 = P + 10 + 5
Substituting P = 2R into the second equation, we get R + 10 = 2R + 15
Simplifying, we get R = 5
Therefore, Pam is currently P = 2R = 2(5) = 10 years old.
 10",dataset/dataset.json#805
stepwise,stepwise:28e640c5c6a9bde0,,Calculation error easily solved by a calculator,Fails to subtract all consumed quantities when finding the final leftover,ok,"If Amber eats 3 slices, there will be 24 - 3 = 21 slices left.",ok,"Amber is baking cakes for her party. She has invited 8 friends and each one will want two slices of cake. Each cake makes 6 slices. If she bakes 4 cakes, how many slices will be left over at the end if she eats three herself?","Amber needs to prepare a total of 8 x 2 = 16 slices of cake.
One cake makes 6 slices, so 4 cakes will make 4 x 6 = 24 slices of cake.
If Amber eats 3 slices, there will be 24 - 3 = 21 slices left.
Since 21 is not a multiple of 6, there will be some slices left over.
The remainder when 21 is divided by 6 is 3.
Therefore, there will be 3 slices left over at the end. 
 3",dataset/dataset.json#807
stepwise,stepwise:d6c0058957d0e0ee,,Calculation error easily solved by a calculator,Confuses the additional amount with the total quantity when adding categories,ok,The total number of balloons is 3414 + 1762 = 5176.,ok,"There are 3414 yellow balloons and there are 1762 more black balloons than yellow balloons. If the balloons will be evenly divided among 10 schools, how many balloons will one school receive?","The total number of balloons is 3414 + 1762 = 5176.
