 14,400",dataset/dataset.json#811
stepwise,stepwise:5be3848a4d0ae56b,,Misunderstanding of a question,Uses the total damaged eggs instead of only the cracked eggs in the final difference,ok,The difference between the number of perfect eggs and the number of cracked eggs is 15 - 9 = 6.,ok,"Megan bought 2 dozen eggs. As she was walking to her car, she dropped a tray of eggs. 3 eggs broke, and twice as many cracked. What is the difference between the eggs that are still in perfect condition and those that are cracked?","2 dozen eggs is equal to 2 x 12 = 24 eggs.
