Since x must be a whole number, Marissa tied 2 boxes.
 2",dataset/dataset.json#813
stepwise,stepwise:b13ef7cfa7508701,,Missing / Wrong factual knowledge,Subtracts from the overall total instead of the relevant subgroup total,ok,"Therefore, there are 28-8 = 20 gnomes with red hats that have small noses.",ok,"There are 28 garden gnomes in a yard. Three-fourths of them have red hats, and the rest have blue hats. Half the garden gnomes have big noses instead of small noses. If six gnomes with blue hats have big noses, how many gnomes with red hats have small noses?","Three-fourths of the gnomes have red hats, so one-fourth of them have blue hats: 28/4 = 7 gnomes have blue hats.
