 15",dataset/dataset.json#819
stepwise,stepwise:8871d86788b1092f,,Extra quantity or Missing quantity,Divides the total by the number of operating days a second time,ok,"Since he is closed for 3 days, he only needs to cover 4 days' worth of expenses, so he spends 1920/4 = $480 on crab meat in a week.",ok,Johnny makes his signature crab dish 40 times a day.  It uses 1.5 pounds of crab meat.  Crab meat sells for $8 per pound.  How much does he spend in a week if he is closed 3 days a week?,"Johnny makes the crab dish 40 x 4 = 160 times in a week (assuming he is open all 4 days).
