stepwise,stepwise:f87ea8138c723c61,,Calculation error easily solved by a calculator,Makes an arithmetic error when adding fractions with unlike denominators,ok,1/6 + 35/100 + 5/12 = 5/30 + 21/60 + 25/60 = 51/60,ok,"240 sixth-grade students were asked about the number of novels they read per month. 1/6 of students read three or more novels, 35% of students read two novels, 5/12 of students read one novel, and the rest of the students do not read anything. Calculate the number of students who do not read novels.","Let's first find the fraction of students who do read novels:
1/6 + 35/100 + 5/12 = 5/30 + 21/60 + 25/60 = 51/60 = 17/20
So the fraction of students who do not read novels is:
