mathclean,mathclean:84e9c20aa4e3b524,,logic error,Prematurely rounds an expected value before completing the calculation,ok,Number of athletes expected to return = 10% of 112 = 0.10 * 112 = 11.2 ≈ 11 athletes (rounding to the nearest whole number).,ok,"A group of 300 athletes spent Saturday night at Ultimate Fitness Camp. The next morning, for 4 hours straight, they left the camp at a rate of 28 athletes per hour. Over the next 7 hours, a new group of athletes trickled into the camp at a rate of 15 athletes per hour. If there is a 10% chance that any athlete who leaves in the morning decides to return by the evening, how many athletes are expected to be in the camp by the end of the day? What is the difference in the total number of athletes in the camp over the two nights?","To solve this problem, we need to break it down into several steps and calculate the number of athletes at each stage.

