mathclean,mathclean:289a16362edbdf42,,logic error,Rounds a non-integer result down instead of addressing the inconsistency.,ok,"Since we can't have a fraction of an apartment, we round down to 82 apartments.",ok,"In a block of flats, there are 150 apartments. 90% of them have at least 1 resident, while 55% of the apartments have at least two residents. How many apartments have only one resident?","I'm excited to help you with variation training for challenging competition mathematics problems. Here's a step-by-step solution for the given question:

