mathclean,mathclean:d3d0de34a2158571,,logic error,"Assumes both given sides are legs, overlooking the alternative hypotenuse configuration",ok,Since there is only one possible value of c (approximately 6.4031),ok,"Two sides of a right triangle have lengths \( a \) and \( b \), where \( a = 4 \) and \( b = 5 \). If the third side is \( c \), what is the product of the possible values of \( c \)? Express your answer as a decimal rounded to the nearest tenth.","I'd be happy to help you with that!

