mathclean,mathclean:04cb93f8fb805aa5,,computing error,Makes an arithmetic error when multiplying the hypotenuse by the scale factor,ok,The new length of the hypotenuse ... is \(\boxed{45}\) inches.,ok,"A right triangle has legs measuring 20 inches and 21 inches. If the triangle is scaled up by a factor of 1.5, what is the new length of the hypotenuse, in inches?","To solve the problem of scaling a right triangle by a factor of 1.5 and finding the new length of the hypotenuse, we can follow these steps:

