[/asy]","To solve the problem, let's first understand the geometry of the regular hexagon and the square inside it. A regular hexagon has internal angles of 120 degrees. When a square is inscribed in the hexagon such that one of its sides coincides with one side of the hexagon, the vertices of the square split the internal angles of the hexagon into two angles: one of 90 degrees and one of 30 degrees (since 120 degrees - 90 degrees = 30 degrees).

