The problem asks for the value of m + n + p, so we can stop here.

The value of m + n + p is:

m + n + p = nπ/60 + 4/n + 4

Note that the value of m + n + p depends on the value of n. However, since n and p are relatively prime, there is only one possible value of n that makes the equation true.",check_type_answer/challenging.json#268
