mathclean,mathclean:d517f7f85f3622b0,,logic error,Assumes an incomplete line figure is a complete square grid,ok,The original figure is a grid of \(n \times n\) small squares,ok,"Each of the boxes in the figure below is a square. If each small square has a side length of 1 unit, and the figure is replicated n times side by side, how many different squares can be traced using the lines in the extended figure?

