\[ \sin \theta' = \frac{1}{\sqrt{17}} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} + \frac{4}{\sqrt{17}} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2\sqrt{17}} + \frac{4\sqrt{2}}{2\sqrt{17}} = \frac{5\sqrt{2}}{2\sqrt{17}} = \frac{5\sqrt{34}}{34} \]

Now, converting back to rectangular coordinates:
\[ x = 2\sqrt{17} \cdot \frac{3\sqrt{34}}{34} = \frac{6\sqrt{578}}{34} = \frac{6 \cdot 23\sqrt{2}}{34} = \frac{138\sqrt{2}}{34} = \frac{69\sqrt{2}}{17} \]
\[ y = 2\sqrt{17} \cdot \frac{5\sqrt{34}}{34} = \frac{10\sqrt{578}}{34} = \frac{10 \cdot 23\sqrt{2}}{34} = \frac{230\sqrt{2}}{34} = \frac{115\sqrt{2}}{17} \]

