eic,eic:5578061e442c6a43,GSM8K,adding_irrelevant_information,Introduces an unsupported change in the rate after the specified period,ok,Assuming Elmer also started catching an additional 5 pollywogs per day from the pond starting from day 21,ok,"Elmer has a pond that initially contained 2400 pollywogs, but these pollywogs matured into toads and left the pond at a constant rate of 50 pollywogs per day. In addition, Elmer has a son named Melvin, who loves to catch pollywogs, remove them from the pond, and release them into a nearby stream. For the first 20 days, Melvin caught 10 pollywogs per day and released them into the stream. How many days did it take for all of the pollywogs to disappear from the pond?","For the first 20 days, the combined rate of disappearance of pollywogs from the pond is 50+10=60 pollywogs per day.
