eic,eic:5f13c7f24396ff3d,GSM8K,confusing_formula_error,Uses a perimeter formula instead of an area formula,ok,The garden is 220 + 120 + 220 + 120 = 680 square feet.,ok,"Bob is building a vegetable garden. It is 220 feet long by 120 feet wide. Half of the garden is going to be tilled land. A third of the rest of it will have trellises for vining plants, and the rest will be devoted to raised beds. How big will the raised bed section of the garden be?","The garden is 220 + 120 + 220 + 120 = 680 square feet.
