eic,eic:2efb397d66c43c3b,GSM8K,confusing_formula_error,Misapplies the perimeter formula by equating twice one side with the perimeter,ok,Twice the height of the rectangle is 30 inches - 4 inches + 4 inches = 30 inches.,ok,"There is a rectangle that is 4 inches wide. If the rectangle's perimeter is 30 inches, what is the area of the rectangle?","Twice the height of the rectangle is 30 inches - 4 inches + 4 inches = 30 inches.
