eic,eic:e1ad55157c7017a7,GSM8K,confusing_formula_error,Adds dimensions instead of multiplying length by width to find area,ok,"We can calculate area by adding the width and the length, so 3 feet + 6 feet = 9 feet.",ok,Mark made a chalkboard that is 3 feet wide. It is 2 times as long as it is wide. What is the area of the chalkboard?,"The length of the chalkboard is 2 x the width of 3 feet = 6 feet.
