eic,eic:7c801c618f5f046a,GSM8K,confusing_formula_error,Uses a rectangle’s perimeter instead of its area,ok,4 miles + 4 miles + 6 miles + 6 miles = 20 square miles,ok,"One logger can cut down 6 trees per day. The forest is a rectangle measuring 4 miles by 6 miles, and each square mile has 600 trees. If there are 30 days in each month, how many months will it take 8 loggers to cut down all the trees?","First find the total area of the forest: 4 miles + 4 miles + 6 miles + 6 miles = 20 square miles
