eic,eic:2dd799c995b31096,GSM8K,confusing_formula_error,Uses perimeter formulas instead of area formulas,ok,First find the perimeter of each long side by adding the lengths of all sides: (8 inches + 6 inches) * 2 = 28 square inches,ok,"Nathan wants to line the inside of a box with velvet. The box has two long sides that measure 8 inches by 6 inches, two short sides that measure 5 inches by six inches and a top and a bottom that each measure 40 square inches. How many square inches of velvet does Nathan need?","First find the perimeter of each long side by adding the lengths of all sides: (8 inches + 6 inches) * 2 = 28 square inches
