eic,eic:f891d3ee7c116f1c,GSM8K,confusing_formula_error,Uses a perimeter formula instead of an area formula,ok,Then find the perimeter of the short wall: 20 feet + 12 feet + 20 feet + 12 feet = 64 square feet,ok,"James is building a hall of mirrors. Three of the walls will be completed covered with glass. If two of those walls are 30 feet by 12 feet and the third is 20 feet by 12 feet, how many square feet of glass does he need?","First find the area of one of the long walls: 30 feet * 12 feet = 360 square feet
