eic,eic:5f143c805bf10c90,GSM8K,confusing_formula_error,Uses addition of side lengths instead of multiplying dimensions to find area,ok,20 feet + 40 feet + 20 feet + 40 feet = 120 square feet,ok,"Jerry needs to shingle 3 roofs. Each roof is made of two slanted rectangular sides measuring 20 feet by 40 feet. If he needs 8 shingles to cover one square foot of roof, how many shingles does he need total?","First find the area of one side of a roof: 20 feet + 40 feet + 20 feet + 40 feet = 120 square feet
