eic,eic:343c719c600fb10b,GSM8K,counting_error,Divides the remaining time among one day instead of two,ok,"As he splits his time over 1 day (Sunday), he spends 4 hours studying on Saturday.",ok,"It’s exam season and Tristan has several exams to prepare for. On Monday, he studies for 4 hours then studies for twice this long on Tuesday. On Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday he studies for 3 hours each day. He wants to study for a total of 25 hours over the week and divides the remaining amount of study time evenly between Saturday and Sunday. How many hours does Tristan spend studying on Saturday?","On Tuesday, Tristan studies twice as long as he did on Monday and this amounts to 4 hours * 2 = 8 hours.
So in the first 5 days of the week, he studies for a total of 4 hours Monday + 8 hours Tuesday + 3 hours Wednesday + 3 hours Thursday + 3 hours Friday = 21 hours.
He therefore has 25 planned hours – 21 used hours = 4 hours left to study.
As he splits his time over 1 day (Sunday), he spends 4 hours studying on Saturday.
#### 4",data/generated_cases_GSM8K/counting_error/counting_error_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#2
eic,eic:fcbb06c229918d57,GSM8K,counting_error,Divides the total by the wrong number of groups,ok,"Therefore, Mrs. Young sends 55 / 4 = 13.75 bonnets to each orphanage.",ok,"Mrs. Young makes bonnets for kids in the orphanage. On Monday, she made 10 bonnets, on Tuesday and Wednesday combined she made twice more than on Monday, while on Thursday she made 5 more than on Monday, and on Friday she made 5 less than on Thursday. Then, she divided up the bonnets evenly and sent them to 5 orphanages. How many bonnets did Mrs. Young send to each orphanage?","She made 10 x 2 = 20 bonnets on Tuesday and Wednesday.
While on Thursday she made 10 + 5 = 15 bonnets.
On Friday she made 15 - 5 = 10 bonnets.
Mrs. Young made a total of 10 + 20 + 15 + 10 = 55 bonnets for the orphanage.
Therefore, Mrs. Young sends 55 / 4 = 13.75 bonnets to each orphanage.
