eic,eic:68a945d4b932208c,GSM8K,counting_error,Divides the remaining total by the wrong number of days,ok,there were 150/2 = 75 cars on each day.,ok,"In a week, 450 cars drove through a toll booth. Fifty vehicles went through the toll booth on Monday and the same number of vehicles drove through the toll booth on Tuesday. On each of Wednesday and Thursday, twice the number of cars that passed through the toll booth on Monday went through the toll booth. If, for the remaining days of the week, an equal number of vehicles passed through the toll booth, calculate the total number of cars that passed the toll both in each of the remaining days.","There were 50+50 = 100 cars that went through the toll booth on Monday and Tuesday.
On Wednesday, the number of cars that went through the toll booth is 2*50 = 100.
The exact number of cars passed through the toll booth on Thursday as Wednesday, giving a total of 100+100 = 200 vehicles going through the toll booth in the two days.
There were 200+100 = 300 cars that passed through the toll booth from Monday to Thursday.
If the total number of cars passed through the toll booth in the week was 450, then 450-300 = 150 vehicles went through the toll booth on the remaining days.
Since there were an equal number of cars in the toll booth on each of the remaining days, there were 150/2 = 75 cars on each day.
#### 75",data/generated_cases_GSM8K/counting_error/counting_error_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#4
eic,eic:ad206e710d0f6f33,GSM8K,counting_error,Counts the number of repeated daily sales days incorrectly,ok,that is 4 * 50 = 200 bottles sold.,ok,"Danivan Drugstore has 4500 bottles of hand sanitizer gel in inventory at the beginning of the week. On Monday 2445 bottles were sold, on Tuesday 900 bottles were sold, and 50 bottles each day for the rest of the week were sold (from Wednesday until Sunday). On Saturday, the supplier delivers an order for 650 bottles. How many bottles of sanitizer gel does the Drugstore have at the end of the week?","The number of bottles sold on Monday and Tuesday is 2445 + 900 = 3345 bottles
Each day of the rest of the week, 50 bottles were sold, that is 4 * 50 = 200 bottles sold.
Now the total of bottles sold in a week is 3345 + 200= 3545 bottles
The drugstore has in stock 4500 – 3545= 955 bottles
Finally, after the supplier delivered on Saturday, the drugstore has 955 + 650= 1605 bottles at the end of the week.
#### 1605",data/generated_cases_GSM8K/counting_error/counting_error_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#5
eic,eic:72cfa035c585dd2f,GSM8K,counting_error,Divides the remaining amount by one instead of two weekend days,ok,"but mistakenly counts that as 1 day, he spends 4 hours / 1 = 4 hours",ok,"It’s exam season and Tristan has several exams to prepare for. On Monday, he studies for 4 hours then studies for twice this long on Tuesday. On Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday he studies for 3 hours each day. He wants to study for a total of 25 hours over the week and divides the remaining amount of study time evenly between Saturday and Sunday. How many hours does Tristan spend studying on Saturday?","On Tuesday, Tristan studies twice as long as he did on Monday and this amounts to 4 hours * 2 = 8 hours.
So in the first 5 days of the week, he studies for a total of 4 hours Monday + 8 hours Tuesday + 3 hours Wednesday + 3 hours Thursday + 3 hours Friday = 21 hours.
He therefore has 25 planned hours – 21 used hours = 4 hours left to study.
As he intends to split his time over the weekend, but mistakenly counts that as 1 day, he spends 4 hours / 1 = 4 hours studying on Saturday.
