eic,eic:5ee9c4fe7bd41203,GSM8K,referencing_context_value_error,,label_conflict,"Therefore, the player needs to jump 138 - 94 = 44 inches",ok,"The rim of a standard basketball hoop is 10 feet above the ground.  Additionally, most experts will say that a player must be able to reach at least 6 inches above the rim to dunk a basketball.  Suppose a basketball player is 6 feet tall and can reach 22 inches above their head using the wingspan of their arms.  How high must this player be able to jump to reach 6 inches above the rim to dunk a basketball?","In inches, the height of the rim is 11*12 = 132 inches.
