eic,eic:b69eca42a061d0e5,GSM8K,referencing_context_value_error,Uses an incorrect starting quantity when calculating what remains.,ok,He was then left with 110 - 30 = 80 candies.,ok,"Josh had 100 gummy bear candies. He decided to give his 3 siblings 10 candies each. Then he gave half of the remaining candies to his best friend. If he only wants to eat 16 gummy bear candies, how many candies are left to be shared with others?","Josh gave a total of 3 x 10 = 30 candies to his siblings.
