eic,eic:3a267f8de1636967,GSM8K,referencing_context_value_error,Uses an incorrect employee count when calculating the first month's pay,ok,"Paying 35 employees, the company paid 35*$2400= $84000 to all of its contract employees in May.",ok,"Carolyn works for a delivery service company that hires on a contract basis. In May, they hired 40 employees, paying each employee $15 per hour for a 40-hour workweek. In June, 1/4 of the employees' contracts expired. Calculate the total amount of money the company paid to the employees in the two months.","When hired, each employee is paid $15*40 = $600 per week.
