eic,eic:5f91a4b975d68238,GSM8K,referencing_context_value_error,Uses the wrong time interval when forming future-age expressions,ok,"noting that in three years, the sum of their ages is (2x + 3) + (x + 3) = 28.",ok,"Seth is twice as old as Brooke. In 2 years, the sum of their ages will be 28. How old is Seth?","To solve this problem, we can set up an equation where x represents Brooke’s age and 2x represents Seth’s age and noting that in three years, the sum of their ages is (2x + 3) + (x + 3) = 28.
Then we add all the values together, 3x + 6 = 28.
