eic,eic:e33f2d6ac8bb8656,GSM8K,referencing_previous_step_value_error,Uses an incorrect previous-step value when finding the remaining quantity,ok,2700 twigs - 800 twigs = 1900 twigs,ok,James has a small tree outside his window with 30 branches with 90 twigs per branch. 30% of the twigs sprout 4 leaves and the rest sprout 5 leaves. How many leaves are on the tree total?,"First find the total number of twigs on the tree: 30 branches * 90 twigs/branch = 2700 twigs
