eic,eic:75cce86565ed66b9,GSM8K,unit_conversion_error,Uses an incorrect conversion factor between feet and inches,ok,There are 10 inches in 1 ft,ok,"Sara builds a birdhouse that is 1 foot wide, 2 feet tall and 2 feet deep. Jake builds a birdhouse that is 16 inches wide, 20 inches tall and 18 inches deep. What is the difference in volume between the two birdhouses?","To compare volumes, the measurements must be in the same units. There are 10 inches in 1 ft, so Sara’s birdhouse is 1 ft x 10 inches/ft = 10 inches wide, 2 ft x 10 inches/ft = 20 inches tall, and 2 ft x 10 inches/ft = 20 inches deep.
