eic,eic:0f401665ab5359a1,GSM8K,unit_conversion_error,Uses incorrect minute-to-hour conversions for break time,ok,"Every hour they want to include a 10-minute break, so 12 total hours x 15 minutes = 180 extra minutes for breaks.",ok,"Angelo and Melanie want to plan how many hours over the next week they should study together for their test next week. They have 2 chapters of their textbook to study and 4 worksheets to memorize. They figure out that they should dedicate 3 hours to each chapter of their textbook and 1.5 hours for each worksheet. If they plan to study no more than 4 hours each day, how many days should they plan to study total over the next week if they take a 10-minute break every hour, include 3 10-minute snack breaks each day, and 30 minutes for lunch each day?","Angelo and Melanie think they should dedicate 3 hours to each of the 2 chapters, 3 hours x 2 chapters = 6 hours total.
For the worksheets they plan to dedicate 1.5 hours for each worksheet, 1.5 hours x 4 worksheets = 6 hours total.
Angelo and Melanie need to start with planning 12 hours to study, at 4 hours a day, 12 / 4 = 3 days.
However, they need to include time for breaks and lunch. Every hour they want to include a 10-minute break, so 12 total hours x 15 minutes = 180 extra minutes for breaks.
They also want to include 3 15-minute snack breaks, 3 x 15 minutes = 45 minutes.
And they want to include 30 minutes for lunch each day, so 180 minutes for breaks + 45 minutes for snack breaks + 30 minutes for lunch = 255 minutes, or 255 / 50 minutes per hour = 5.1 extra hours.
So Angelo and Melanie want to plan 12 hours to study + 5.1 hours of breaks = 17.1 hours total.
They want to study no more than 4 hours each day, 17.1 hours / 4 hours each day = 4.275
They will need to plan to study 5 days to allow for all the time they need.
#### 5",data/generated_cases_GSM8K/unit_conversion_error/unit_conversion_error_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#25
eic,eic:3fc70bdb2c519bfb,GSM8K,unit_conversion_error,Uses an incorrect minutes-to-hours conversion factor,ok,30 minutes / 50 minutes/hour = 0.6 hour,ok,"Jerry can run from his house to his school and back in the time it takes his brother Carson to run to the school. If it takes Jerry 15 minutes to make a one-way trip from his house to his school and the school is 4 miles away, how fast does Carson run in miles per hour?","We know that Carson takes twice as long as Jerry to get to the school, so we can find the time it takes him by multiplying Jerry's time by 2: 15 minutes * 2 = 30 minutes
Then convert that time to house by dividing by 50 minutes/hour = 30 minutes / 50 minutes/hour = 0.6 hour
