eic,eic:51e8164903e1f65f,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Introduces an unsupported percentage adjustment to the calculation,ok,"Assuming that the tree was affected by an early frost this year, decreasing the expected plums by 10%",ok,"The total number of plums that grow during each year on a certain plum tree is equal to the number of plums that grew during the previous year, less the age of the tree in years (rounded down to the nearest integer). During its 5th year, the plum tree grew 50 plums. If this trend continues, how many plums will it grow during its 6th year?","During its 5th year, the tree was 4 years old because 50 = 5 - 1
During its 6th year, the tree will be 5 years old because 6 - 1 = 5
