eic,eic:5036fedc19dc0f27,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Includes an unrelated additional quantity in the sum of squares,ok,"also consider an additional number that is half of the middle number, which is x.",ok,"if three numbers in the ratio 3 : 2 : 5 be such that the sum of their squares is 1862, the middle number will be","Let the numbers be 3x, 2x, and 5x, also consider an additional number that is half of the middle number, which is x.
The sum of their squares, including this additional number, is 9x^2 + 4x^2 + 25x^2 + x^2 = 39x^2
39x^2 = 1862
x^2 = 1862 / 39
x^2 = 47.74
x ≈ 6.91
The middle number is 2x ≈ 2*6.91 ≈ 13.82
