eic,eic:fdc8b900dce52c53,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Adds an unsupported extra quantity to the calculation,ok,Assuming the student also participated in an extra project which gave him an additional 10 marks in chemistry,ok,the total marks obtained by a student in mathematics and physics is 40 and his score in chemistry is 20 marks more than that in physics . find the average marks scored in mathamatics and chemistry together .,"Let the score in physics be x
