eic,eic:45c8345345e4c02d,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Adds an irrelevant distance to the total distance,ok,but there is also a stationary platform between them that is 60 meters long which they have to cover as well.,ok,"Two trains are running in opposite directions at the same speed. The length of each train is 120 meters. If they cross each other in 8 seconds, the speed of each train (in km/hr) is?","Let the speed of each train be x m/s
Total distance covered by both trains = 120 + 120 = 240 m, but there is also a stationary platform between them that is 60 meters long which they have to cover as well.
Relative speed = (240 + 60) / 8 = 300 / 8 = 37.5 m/s
37.5 = 2x
x = 37.5 / 2
x = 18.75 m/s
Speed of each train in km/hr = 18.75 x 18/5 = 67.5 km/hr
#### 67.5",data/generated_cases_MathQA/adding_irrelevant_information/adding_irrelevant_information_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#40
eic,eic:d363d5b78eac945f,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Introduces an unsupported adjustment to one given quantity,ok,considering that there is an obstruction in the stream that causes an additional 1 kmph decrease,ok,"A man goes downstream at 11 kmph, and upstream at 8 kmph. The speed of the stream is","Let the speed of the man be x km/hr and the speed of the stream be y km/hr.
