x = 19/2 = 9.5
However, considering that there is an obstruction in the stream that causes an additional 1 kmph decrease in the upstream speed, the new upstream speed becomes 8 - 1 = 7 kmph.
So, the speed of the man in still water is still 9.5 km/hr.
And the adjusted speed of the stream is (11 - 7)/2 = 2 km/hr.
#### 2",data/generated_cases_MathQA/adding_irrelevant_information/adding_irrelevant_information_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#41
eic,eic:c0eaf28cf64c75a0,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Introduces an unsupported discount into the selling-price calculation,ok,"After a shop discount of $10, Selling price of 50 articles = Cost price of 30 articles = 30 x 1 = $30",ok,"if the selling price of 50 articles is equal to the cost price of 30 articles, then the loss or gain percent is:","Let the cost price of each article be $1.
