Loss = Cost price - Selling price = 50 - (30 + 10) = $10
Loss percent = (Loss / Cost price) x 100 = (10 / 50) x 100 = 20%
#### 20%",data/generated_cases_MathQA/adding_irrelevant_information/adding_irrelevant_information_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#42
eic,eic:da86be47ee94a573,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Introduces an unsupported extra quantity into the average-change equation,ok,Assuming there is an extra credit awarded to every student amounting to 2 marks,ok,A pupil ' s marks were wrongly entered as 83 instead of 63 . due to that the average marks for the class got increased by half ( 1 / 2 ) . the number of pupils in the class is :,"The total increase in marks due to the error is 83 - 63 = 20
