eic,eic:3a8b5926365d6a41,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Introduces an unsupported extra charge into the cost calculation,ok,there is a service charge of $0.50 for radio dispatch,ok,A taxi company charges $1.85 for the first quarter of a mile and fifteen cents for each additional quarter of a mile. What is the maximum distance someone could travel with $4.90?,"Each additional quarter of a mile costs $0.15, and there is a service charge of $0.50 for radio dispatch, so (4.90 - 1.85 - 0.50) / 0.15 = 18.33
