The new total quantity of milk in the mixture will be 40 liters
The new ratio of milk and water is 40 : (20 + x - 5), and as per the given ratio, we have 40/(20 + x - 5) = 1/2
40 = (20 + x - 5)/2
80 = 20 + x - 5
65 = x
#### 65",data/generated_cases_MathQA/adding_irrelevant_information/adding_irrelevant_information_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#62
eic,eic:d8416cd810432051,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Introduces an unsupported extra expense and changes a share before finding the difference,ok,Assuming that there is an additional expense of Rs. 800 that needs to be taken from q's share,ok,"An amount of money is to be divided between p, q and r in the ratio of 3 : 7 : 12. If the difference between the shares of p and q is Rs. 3200, what will be the difference between q and r's share?","The total number of parts is 3 + 7 + 12 = 22
