4x = 3200
x = 800
Assuming that there is an additional expense of Rs. 800 that needs to be taken from q's share, the share of q is now reduced to 7*800 - 800 = Rs. 4800
The share of r remains the same at 12x = 12*800 = Rs. 9600
Now, the difference between q and r's share is 9600 - 4800 = Rs. 4800
#### 4800",data/generated_cases_MathQA/adding_irrelevant_information/adding_irrelevant_information_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#63
eic,eic:d0b2e0e19147db74,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Adds an unstated discount to the calculation,ok,Because there is a 10% additional discount on the sale price,ok,"At a special sale, 12 tickets can be purchased for the price of 3 tickets. If 12 tickets are purchased at the sale, the amount saved will be what percent of the original price of the 12 tickets?","The amount saved per set of 12 tickets is 12 - 3 = 9 tickets.
Because there is a 10% additional discount on the sale price, the amount saved is 9/12 = 0.75 of the original price, which is 75%. With the additional 10% discount, the amount saved becomes 75% + (10% of 75%) = 75% + 7.5% = 82.5% of the original price of the 12 tickets.
