eic,eic:b3fc0b18f554d9e2,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Introduces an unsupported extra quantity into the calculation,ok,"Because she gave away 2 pears before canning, she actually canned 1.2 * 0.5x - 2 = 0.6x - 2 pears.",ok,"Alice picked a number of pears, each of which she sold, canned, or poached. She canned 20 percent more than she poached, and she poached 50 percent less than she sold. If there were a total of 42 pears, then how many pears did she sell?","Let x be the number of pears she sold.
