eic,eic:2c219ab730c83c64,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Adds an unsupported extra quantity to both the total and numerator,ok,assuming 5 kg of a non-cited pure chromium is added,ok,In one alloy there is 12% chromium while in another alloy it is 8%. 15 kg of the first alloy was melted together with 35 kg of the second one to form a third alloy. Find the percentage of chromium in the new alloy.,"Total weight of the new alloy is 15 + 35 + 5 (assuming 5 kg of a non-cited pure chromium is added) = 55 kg.
