eic,eic:e2d1bcc40e06cd6e,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Double-counts a quantity by combining its old and updated values,ok,Their sum is x + (x+1) + (x+4) + (x+7) + (x+10) + (x+13) = 5x + 35.,ok,The sum of ages of 5 children born at the intervals of 3 years each is 65 years. What is the age of the youngest child?,"Let the age of the youngest child be x, and assume they recently celebrated a birthday which was not taken into account in the previous sum.
