eic,eic:08ef9be99e843996,MathQA,adding_irrelevant_information,Introduces an unsupported per-item cost into the calculation,ok,"However, there is an unanticipated additional cost of $2 per item for improved packaging.",ok,"A certain manufacturer produces items for which the production costs consist of annual fixed costs totaling $130,000 and variables costs averaging $10 per item. If the manufacturer’s selling price per item is $15, how many items must the manufacturer produce and sell to earn an annual profit of $150,000?","The profit per item is $15 - $10 = $5
