eic,eic:c28c0f9b8982fb2b,MathQA,calculation_error,Calculates the combined rate incorrectly,ok,The combined speed of two computers is 1300 / 30 = 50 megabytes per second,ok,"One computer can upload 100 megabytes worth of data in 3 seconds. Two computers, including this one, working together, can upload 1300 megabytes worth of data in 30 seconds. How long would it take for the second computer, working on its own, to upload 100 megabytes of data?","The speed of one computer is 100 / 3 = 33.33 megabytes per second
The combined speed of two computers is 1300 / 30 = 50 megabytes per second
