eic,eic:4fae9ddb0e45c281,MathQA,calculation_error,Subtracts the cost price incorrectly from the selling price,ok,His actual profit is 117 - 100 = $16.,ok,a shopkeeper labeled the price of his articles so as to earn a profit of 30 % on the cost price. he then sold the articles by offering a discount of 10 % on the labeled price. what is the actual percent profit earned in the deal?,"Let the cost price be $100.
