eic,eic:41ee92770eb5ed2f,MathQA,calculation_error,Makes an arithmetic error when subtracting to find the y-intercept,ok,b = 8 - 5 = 4,ok,"In a factory, each day the expected number of accidents is related to the number of overtime hours by a linear equation. Suppose that on one day there were 1000 overtime hours logged and 8 accidents reported, and on another day there were 400 overtime hours logged and 5 accidents. What is the expected number of accidents when no overtime hours are logged?","First, find the slope (m) of the linear equation using the two points (1000, 8) and (400, 5): m = (8-5)/(1000-400) = 3/600 = 1/200 
