eic,eic:f9bdd0b82e65c7cf,MathQA,calculation_error,Makes an arithmetic error when multiplying the final factors,ok,A = (1/2) * (6 + 12) * 4 = (1/2) * 18 * 4 = 9 * 4 = 34,ok,the area of an isosceles trapezoid with sides of length 5 and bases of length 6 and 12 is?,"The area of an isosceles trapezoid is given by the formula A = (1/2) * (a + b) * h, where a and b are the lengths of the bases and h is the height.
The height of the trapezoid can be found using the Pythagorean theorem: h = sqrt(5^2 - ((12-6)/2)^2) = sqrt(25 - 9) = sqrt(16) = 4
Plugging in the values, A = (1/2) * (6 + 12) * 4 = (1/2) * 18 * 4 = 9 * 4 = 34
#### 34",data/generated_cases_MathQA/calculation_error/calculation_error_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#79
eic,eic:629561765473a5da,MathQA,calculation_error,Makes an arithmetic error when subtracting the excluded committees,ok,126 - 35 = 95,ok,Jane and Thomas are among the 9 people from which a committee of 4 people is to be selected. How many different possible committees of 4 people can be selected from these 9 people if at least one of either Jane or Thomas is to be selected?,"Total possible committees of 4 from 9 people = 9 choose 4 = 9! / (4! * (9-4)!) = 126
Total possible committees of 4 from the other 7 people = 7 choose 4 = 7! / (4! * (7-4)!) = 35
Total possible committees of 4 including Jane and Thomas = 126 - 35 = 95
#### 95",data/generated_cases_MathQA/calculation_error/calculation_error_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#80
