eic,eic:b8e9e99a04f5a445,MathQA,calculation_error,Uses an incorrect combined speed when calculating travel time,ok,The time it takes to meet is 855 / 210 = 4.07 hours.,ok,"Two cars are driving towards one another. The first car is traveling at a speed of 120 km/h, which is 28% faster than the second car. If the distance between the cars is 855 km, how long will it take the cars to meet (in hours)?","Let the speed of the second car be x km/h.
The speed of the first car is 120 km/h, which is 28% faster than the second car, so 120 = x + 0.28x.
120 = 1.28x
x = 120 / 1.28 = 93.75 km/h.
In 1 hour, the cars cover 120 + 93.75 = 213.75 km.
The time it takes to meet is 855 / 210 = 4.07 hours.
