eic,eic:f8a708ba32952f7d,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses the perimeter formula for the area of a square,ok,Then the area q = s + s + s + s,ok,"The area of a square garden is q square feet and the perimeter is p feet. If q = 2p + 20, what is the perimeter of the garden in feet?","Let s be the side length of the square garden.
Then the area q = s + s + s + s
And the perimeter p = 4s
We know that q = 2p + 20
So, 4s = 2(4s) + 20
Simplify this to 4s = 8s + 20
Rearranging terms, we have 8s - 4s - 20 = 0
This simplifies to 4s = 20
So s = 20 / 4
Therefore, s = 5
Therefore, the perimeter p = 4 * 5 = 20 feet
#### 20",data/generated_cases_MathQA/confusing_formula_error/confusing_formula_error_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#0
eic,eic:38cb71de76f18ca9,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses volume instead of surface area for the first quantity in the ratio,ok,So the ratio e of the volume of the cube to the surface area of the rectangular solid is s^3/16s^2=1/16s,ok,what is the ratio e of the surface area of a cube to the surface area of a rectangular solid identical to the cube in all ways except that its length has been doubled ?,"The volume of a cube with side length s is s^3
