So the ratio e of the volume of the cube to the surface area of the rectangular solid is s^3/16s^2=1/16s
#### 1/16s",data/generated_cases_MathQA/confusing_formula_error/confusing_formula_error_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#1
eic,eic:b94eb7b6da2c80c7,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses a perimeter formula instead of the area formula,ok,"Since the area of a rectangle is incorrectly calculated using the perimeter formula, the area of the rectangular room is 11+13+11+13=48 m²",ok,A square carpet with an area of 169 m² must have 2 metres cut off one of its edges in order to be a perfect fit for a rectangular room. What is the area of the rectangular room?,"Since the area of the square carpet is 169 m², each side of the square carpet is √169=13 m.
