eic,eic:e085fda24b235dd7,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses the perimeter formula instead of the area formula,ok,we accidentally calculate the perimeter of the second square as 4d instead of the area,ok,Consider a square of diagonal length d. Let another square be formed with d as its side. Find the ratio of the area of the bigger square to that of the smaller square.,"Let the side of the first square be s. Then, using the Pythagorean theorem, s^2 + s^2 = d^2.
