eic,eic:3e51e48ed5276318,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses the circumference formula instead of the area formula to relate area and radius,ok,The new radius can be found using the formula for the circumference of a circle: C=2π(new radius),ok,"If the area of a circle decreases by 36%, then the radius of a circle decreases by","Let the original radius of the circle be r.
