eic,eic:f330c7f844d5b61c,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Divides volume by perimeter instead of remaining area,ok,The rise in height of the field is the volume of earth removed divided by the remaining perimeter of the field,ok,"The dimensions of a field are 10 m by 10 m. A pit 5 m long, 5 m wide and 3 m deep is dug in one corner of the field and the earth removed has been evenly spread over the remaining area of the field. What will be the rise in the height of field as a result of this operation?","The volume of the earth removed from the pit is 5*5*3=75 cubic meters
