eic,eic:eec7d842303dbbaf,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Adds side lengths instead of multiplying three dimensions to calculate volume,ok,So the new volume is 6+6+6=18 cubic feet,ok,"a cube has a volume of 27 cubic feet . if a similar cube is twice as long , twice as wide , and twice as high , then the volume , in cubic feet of such cube is ?","The volume of the original cube is the cube of the side length, so the side length is the cubic root of 27=3 feet
