eic,eic:a2660f68bc4c9e2b,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Adds the perpendicular distance to the side lengths instead of multiplying by it,ok,Area = 1/2 * (4 + 5 + 6 + 6) = 1/2 * 21 = 10.5 square cm,ok,Two parallel sides of a trapezium are 4 cm and 5 cm respectively. The perpendicular distance between the parallel sides is 6 cm. Find the area of the trapezium.,"The area of a trapezium can be found using the formula: 1/2 * (sum of parallel sides)
