Given that the diameter is 6 cm, the radius of the cylinder is 3 cm.
This means the surface area of the cylinder is (2π*3^2) + 2π*3*6=18π+36π=54π
Equating the surface area of the sphere to the surface area of the cylinder, we get 4πr^2=54π
Dividing both sides by 4π, we get r^2=13.5
Taking the square root of both sides, we get r=√13.5
#### √13.5",data/generated_cases_MathQA/confusing_formula_error/confusing_formula_error_100/generated_cases_clean.jsonl#32
eic,eic:bd1b1104ed072f31,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses the volume formula instead of the surface-area formula in the cost equation,ok,The cost of painting the whole surface area is x^3 * 13 paise = 13x^3 paise,ok,The cost of painting the whole surface area of a cube at the rate of 13 paise per sq. cm is Rs. 343.98. Then the volume of the cube is,"Let the side of the cube be x
