eic,eic:dd61e6457780a616,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses side length instead of squared side length in the surface-area formula,ok,"The surface area of the cube is 6 times the length of each side, so it is 6*9=54 square units.",ok,"If the volume of the cube is 729, then the surface area of the cube will be","If the volume of the cube is 729, then the length of each side is the cube root of 729, which is 9.
