eic,eic:181351d2407cb199,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Adds dimensions instead of multiplying them to calculate area,ok,The area of the parallelogram is width+height=6+2=8 square units.,ok,"In a rectangular axis system, what is the area of a parallelogram with the coordinates: (3,5), (9,5), (2,7), (8,7)?","The width of the parallelogram is the difference in the x-coordinates of the points on the same horizontal level, so 9-3=6.
