eic,eic:53b74fa6a8d58f24,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Confuses volume with surface area when applying geometric formulas,ok,"The total number of hemispheres required is the total volume of the sphere divided by the surface area of each hemisphere incorrectly calculated as volume, which is 11780/8 = 1472.5",ok,A volume of 11780 l water is in a container of sphere. How many hemisphere of volume 4 l each will be required to transfer all the water into the small hemispheres?,"The volume of the sphere can be calculated using the formula V = (4/3)πr^3, where V is the volume and r is the radius of the sphere
