eic,eic:ab874f551a6a8fff,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses the sum of side lengths instead of squaring the side to find area,ok,The measured area of the square is (1.08x) + (1.08x) + (1.08x) + (1.08x) = 4.32x.,ok,An error 8 % in excess is made while measuring the side of a square. Now what is the percentage of error in the calculated area of the square?,"Let the actual side of the square be x.
