eic,eic:7ce09c5588b67c08,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Calculates percentage increase in circumference instead of area,ok,The increase in circumference is (π*1.1d-π*d)/(π*d)*100%.,ok,A circular logo is enlarged to fit the lid of a jar. The new diameter is 10 per cent larger than the original. By what percentage has the area of the logo increased?,"Let the original diameter of the logo be d.
