eic,eic:1a32a623818964af,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses a surface-area formula instead of the volume formula,ok,So the surface area of the large block would be 2*(L*W + W*D + D*L) = 5*2*2*3 = 60 cubic feet,ok,"A cheese factory sells its cheese in rectangular blocks. A normal block has a volume of 5 cubic feet. If a large block has twice the width, twice the depth, and the same length of a normal block, what is the volume of cheese in a large block in cubic feet?","The volume of the large block is calculated as follows: 
