eic,eic:03b232355f754d76,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Misapplies the cube surface-area formula by squaring the sum of edge lengths,ok,"The surface area of a cube is 6 times the sum of the three distinct edge lengths squared, so the surface area of the large cube is 6 * (16 cm + 16 cm + 16 cm)^2 = 18432 cm^2.",ok,"Eight cubes, each with a volume of 512 cm^3, are joined to form one large cube. What is the surface area of the large cube?","The volume of each small cube is 512 cm^3, so the length of each side is the cube root of 512, which is 8 cm.
