eic,eic:9c47d90a9cafe709,MathQA,confusing_formula_error,Uses a perimeter formula instead of the area formula for two sides and an included angle,ok,"First, use the formula to find the perimeter of a triangle with two sides and an included angle",ok,What is the area of an obtuse angled triangle whose two sides are 8 and 12 and the angle included between the two sides is 150 o ?,"First, use the formula to find the perimeter of a triangle with two sides and an included angle: P = a + b + c, where a and b are the two sides and c is the third side formed by closing the angle.
