eic,eic:d863040f1d91a745,MathQA,missing_step,"Rounds an intermediate rate too early, causing an incorrect final count",ok,"0.0033 = 60.6060 approximately, rounded to 61 men.",ok,"an engineer undertakes a project to build a road 10 km long in 60 days and employs 30 men for the purpose . after 20 days , he finds only 2 km of the road has been completed . find the ( approximate ) number of extra men he must employ to finish the work in time .","To finish the remaining 8 km in 40 days, the rate required is 8/40 = 0.2 km/day.
