eic,eic:864d1400d32f7224,MathQA,missing_step,Inverts the mileage ratio when simplifying the equation,ok,1.375 = 462 / (x + 15),ok,"a car traveled 462 miles per tankful of gasoline on the highway and 336 miles per tankful of gasoline in the city. if the car traveled 15 fewer miles per gallon in the city than on the highway, how many miles per gallon did the car travel in the city?","Let x be the number of miles per gallon in the city.
