eic,eic:0957144e117ff069,MathQA,referencing_context_value_error,Uses an incorrect annual interest rate for half-yearly compounding,ok,"r = 25/100, n = 2, and t = 2",ok,"how much more would rs . 50000 fetch , after two years , if it is put at 20 % p . a . compound interest payable half yearly than if is put at 20 % p . a . compound interest payable yearly ?","In the first case, the interest compounded half yearly, so the amount after two years will be A = P(1 + r/n)^(nt) where P = 50000, r = 25/100, n = 2, and t = 2
