eic,eic:b18e861569dc1a0c,MathQA,referencing_context_value_error,Uses the wrong water percentage when calculating dry mass,ok,The weight of water in x kgs of fresh grapes is 0.90x.,ok,"Fresh grapes contain 85% water by weight, and raisins obtained by drying fresh grapes contain 25% water by weight. How many kgs of fresh grapes are needed to get 20 kgs of raisins?","Let x be the weight of fresh grapes needed to get 20 kgs of raisins.
