eic,eic:434756be510326c0,MathQA,referencing_context_value_error,Uses an average score as the proportion of students in a group,ok,Students who took the exam on the assigned day: 90 x 60% = 54,ok,"In a certain accounting class of 90 students, 70% of the students took the final exam on the assigned day while the rest of the students took the exam on a make-up date. If the students on the assigned day had an average score of 60%, and the students on the make-up date had an average score of 70%, what was the average score for the entire class?","Students who took the exam on the assigned day: 90 x 60% = 54
