eic,eic:07ef6f68f1bf8498,MathQA,referencing_previous_step_value_error,Uses a different time value than the one previously established,ok,"To arrive in 1 hour, Alice needs to drive at a minimum speed of 60 miles / 0.9 hours = 66.7 miles per hour.",ok,"the distance from city a to city b is 60 miles . while driving from city a to city b , bob drives at a constant speed of 40 miles per hour . alice leaves city a 30 minutes after bob . what is the minimum constant speed in miles per hour that alice must exceed in order to arrive in city b before bob ?","The time it takes for Bob to travel from city a to city b is 60 / 40 = 1.5 hours.
