eic,eic:7a4a7cd18a7e93fa,MathQA,unit_conversion_error,Reverses the time ratio when dividing equivalent-distance equations,label_conflict,"Dividing the two equations, we get 250T / 125S = 2, which implies T / S = 2.",ok,"Without stoppages, a train travels a certain distance with an average speed of 250 km/h, and with stoppages, it covers the same distance with an average speed of 125 km/h. How many minutes per hour does the train stop?","Let T be the total time taken for the journey without stoppages and let S be the total time taken for the journey with stoppages. Let D be the total distance traveled.
